    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "University Of The Incarnate Word: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.uiw.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University Of The Incarnate Word: All Jobs 2026-06-02T10:04:46-05:00 https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31113 2026-06-02T10:04:45-05:00 2026-06-02T10:04:46-05:00 UIW Community Clinic Office Assistant <div>The UIW Community Clinic Office Assistant will act as the UIW Community Clinic Floor Manager to assist in supervising physical therapist(s), clinic administrators, students, and patients/clients with all clinic duties.&nbsp; The UIW Community Clinic Office Assistant reports to the UIW Community Clinic Lead.</div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31555 2026-07-30T10:14:22-05:00 2026-07-30T10:14:23-05:00 Lead Lab Teaching Assistant <div>The Lead Lab Teaching Assistant (TA) assists current RSO students with lab tutoring for the following courses: Clinical Optometry I, Clinical Optometry II, Clinical Optometry III, Clinical Optometry IV, Neuroanatomy lab and any other labs as needed. Additionally, the Lead TA performs administrative duties in scheduling and communicating with Lab TA's while ensuring smooth functioning of the labs.</div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30869 2026-04-16T09:34:39-05:00 2026-04-16T09:34:40-05:00 Communication Arts Part-Time Lecturer-Film Studies Spring 2027 <div>The Department of Communication Arts in the School of Media &amp; Design is seeking part-time faculty candidates for Communication Arts Lecturer in Film Studies for spring 2027. Position will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in this discipline. The courses span the field of film studies, including: history of film, film criticism and analysis, film theory, and genre studies. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31337 2026-07-02T23:21:18-05:00 2026-07-02T23:21:19-05:00 Student Technician for Sports and Wellness <div>The Student Technician for Sports and Wellness is responsible for completing maintenance and repairs of equipment and facility for Sports and Wellness Facilities, including, Wellness Center, Natatorium, and Fencing Center. Duties for this position include daily cleaning of the facility, equipment, and dressing rooms. The Student Technician for Sports and Wellness reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.</div><div><br></div><div><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested UIW students as the need arises.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31718 2026-08-25T10:01:32-05:00 2026-08-25T10:01:32-05:00 Lecturer in Communications-SPS <div>The School of Professional Studies invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Communications. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for 2026-2027 academic year. Note that part-time faculty are assigned for one term at a time.</em></strong></div> School of Professional Studies https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31299 2026-06-30T09:38:36-05:00 2026-06-30T09:38:37-05:00 Senior Student Account Representative <div>The Senior Student Account Representative is responsible for serving as the primary point of contact to students and parents with respect to student finances, billing, third party billing and payment options. The Senior Student Account Representative (SSAR) is part of an outstanding team responsible for providing excellent service to students, parents, staff, and faculty. The Senior Student Account Representative reports to the Director of the Business Office.</div> Business Office https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31622 2026-08-12T15:15:24-05:00 2026-08-12T15:15:25-05:00 Charter Bus Driver <div>The Charter Bus Driver is responsible for safely operating a gas or diesel bus on routes for the University, observing all state and city speed and safety regulations. Position is also responsible for providing excellent customer service to passengers and following safety policies of the University. The Charter Bus Driver reports to Vehicle Services Manager.<br><br><strong><em>Position requires the ability to successfully pass a required DOT physical.</em></strong></div> Vehicle Operations https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31021 2026-05-13T20:53:14-05:00 2026-05-13T20:53:14-05:00 SRS Research Graduate Assistant <div>The Research Graduate Assistant for the School of Rehabilitation Sciences will work with a SRS faculty member or administrator in dedicated line of scholarly work. Selected applicants will participate in project development, literature review, project execution, and data analysis and synthesis.. The Research Graduate Assistant reports to the Dean of the School of Rehabilitation Sciences.</div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31448 2026-07-14T16:35:44-05:00 2026-07-14T16:35:44-05:00 Graduate Assistant Cheer Coach <div>The Graduate Assistant Cheer Coach is responsible for coaching the cheer program at the University of the Incarnate Word including tryouts, training, coordination, and scheduling as well as game-day responsibilities including but not limited to; performances, pre-game and in-game appearances, half time performances. This position will also assist in the try outs, training and coordination of the mascot. This position reports to the Student-Athlete Development Coordinator. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31763 2026-09-01T16:23:28-05:00 2026-09-01T16:23:29-05:00 Administrative Coordinator-Unified In Wellness (Part Time) <div>The Administrative Coordinator-Unified In Wellness (PT) is responsible for providing administrative support for the Unified-In-Wellness program to ensure all daily procedures run smoothly. The Administrative Coordinator-Unified In Wellness (PT) reports to the Associate Provost for HP Initiatives and Partnerships.</div> Office of the Provost https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30676 2026-03-19T08:37:24-05:00 2026-03-19T08:37:25-05:00 Clinical & Applied Science Education (CASE) Coordinator <div>The CASE Coordinator is responsible for administrative support to the Senior Associate Dean, Department Chairs of CASE and Faculty of UIWSOM. The CASE Coordinator will work directly with the Dean’s office regarding policies and procedures related to faculty and assists with notification and implementation of approved policies. The CASE Coordinator reports to the Senior Associate Dean of Academic Affairs (SADAA) at the School of Osteopathic Medicine (SOM). <br><br><em>The University of the Incarnate Word School of Osteopathic Medicine educates aspiring physicians to be justice-minded, global citizens using a community-based, distributed model of education, which fosters inclusion, discovery and innovation. The UIWSOM welcomes applications for the Clinical &amp; Applied Science Education (CASE) Coordinator Position.</em></div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31720 2026-08-25T10:06:34-05:00 2026-08-25T10:06:35-05:00 High School Counselor <div>St. Anthony Catholic High School, a private, college preparatory High school for young men and women, is seeking a High School Counselor. The Counselor is responsible for supporting all St. Anthony Catholic High School (SACHS) students in their social, emotional, academic, college, and career development. Position will ensure students receive the courses required to meet graduation requirements for their proposed endorsement, as well as assist in planning the campus master schedule. All staff are expected to work within the mission of SACHS and our Core Values of Honesty &amp; Integrity; Community; Service &amp; Social Justice; Scholarship; and Holistic Education. The Counselor reports to the High School Principal.<br><br><em>St. Anthony Catholic High School prepares young men and women for positions of responsibility and leadership through a college preparatory curriculum based on Catholic values and traditions.</em></div> St. Anthony Catholic High School https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31135 2026-06-05T09:13:53-05:00 2026-06-05T09:13:54-05:00 Campus Life Assistant (Work-Study) <div>The Student Assistant for Campus Life works in conjunction with all Campus Life offices and is aware of all services provided by Campus Life, Campus Engagement, and Student Advocacy offices to better serve students and visitors. The Office of Campus Life is a high traffic, high volume, high call area and assistance within all departments is shared to provide a customer-friendly environment to all students and visitors to the Office of Campus Life. The Campus Life Office Assistant reports to Secretary/Office Coordinator.<br><br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Campus Engagement https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31557 2026-07-30T10:53:28-05:00 2026-07-30T10:53:28-05:00 Graduate Assistant for Media Relations <div>The Graduate Assistant for Media Relations is responsible for contributions to the University’s athletics website and serving as the primary contact for assigned sports while assisting with other sports. This position will support the communications department by monitoring, updating, editing, and proof-reading recaps, articles, game and year stats, and social media information. The Graduate Assistant reports to Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing.</div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30877 2026-04-16T17:30:34-05:00 2026-04-16T17:30:34-05:00 Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant <div>The Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant is responsible for duties including but not limited to assistance with travel plans, set up for games &amp; practices, managing equipment, game and practice video, on-court duties, social media, community service, and organizing team events. The Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant reports to the Head Women's Basketball Coach.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31339 2026-07-02T23:46:29-05:00 2026-07-02T23:46:30-05:00 Communications Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Communications Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for assisting in all aspects of Sports and Wellness communication, including website maintenance and development, video/multimedia production, social media engagement, and promotions. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.</div><div><br></div><div><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></div><div><br>&nbsp;<br><br></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30708 2026-03-24T15:05:32-05:00 2026-03-24T15:05:32-05:00 The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist <div>The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist (MMJ) helps the editor and assistant editor, in producing The Logos, the student-run digital newspaper. The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist reports to the Faculty Advisor for The Logos.<br><br>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired<br>through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31319 2026-07-02T08:44:45-05:00 2026-07-02T08:44:46-05:00 Student Office Assistant (Work-Study) <div>The Student Office Assistant assists in the daily operations of the School of Mathematics, Science, and Engineering Dean's Office. The Student Office Assistant reports to the Administrative Assistant to the Dean.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31628 2026-08-14T17:35:16-05:00 2026-08-14T17:35:16-05:00 Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability-Student Assistant <div>The Student Assistant for the Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability provides clerical &amp; programmatic support, including but not limited to: assisting office staff with mass marketing/publications/mail-outs, data entry, filing, customer service, social media &amp; program support. The Student Assistant reports to the Director for the Ettling Center.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31023 2026-05-13T21:27:38-05:00 2026-05-13T21:27:39-05:00 RLHO Graduate Assistant - Housing Operations <div>The RLHO Graduate Assistant is considered essential personnel and works under the supervision of the Residence Life &amp; Housing Operations (RLHO) full-time staff to support students and student staff by providing a holistic, high-quality residential living experience. Expectations include ability to recruit, train, and mentor student staff on community policies, operational procedures, crisis response, and professional development. The RLHO Graduate Assistant reports to the Associate Director of Residence Life &amp; Housing Operations<br><br></div><div>As a 12-month live-in leadership member, the <strong><em>GA-Housing Operations</em></strong> is primarily responsible for overseeing maintenance and aesthetics of the residential community at UIW, managing occupancy, and assisting with large scale departmental operations events (in conjunction with full-time staff).</div> Residence Life & Housing Operations https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31473 2026-07-17T14:58:42-05:00 2026-07-17T14:58:42-05:00 Graduate Assistant for Women's Tennis <div>The Graduate Assistant for Women's Tennis provides support to the Head Coach in all aspects of academic success, coaching, strength, conditioning, recruiting, planning of practice, organization of team meetings, scheduling and trip management. The Graduate Assistant for Women's Tennis reports to the Head Coach for Women's Tennis. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW grauate students.</em></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31775 2026-09-04T08:09:04-05:00 2026-09-04T08:09:05-05:00 Parking Services Liaison-PT <div>The Parking Services Liaison enforces traffic and parking regulations, assists in special events, and reports all irregularities, emergencies, or suspicious activity to the University Police Department. The Parking Services Liaison will report to the University Police Lieutenant.<br><strong><em><br>This is a part-time position that works 29 hours per week for 10 months out of the year.</em></strong></div> University Police https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31341 2026-07-02T23:51:07-05:00 2026-07-02T23:51:08-05:00 Club Sport Athletic Trainer (Graduate Assistant) <div>Club Sport Athletic Trainer (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for assisting in the development, direction, and evaluation of a comprehensive athletic training Club Sports program. Coordinates and delivers athletic training services to various club student-athletes. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31726 2026-08-27T08:16:00-05:00 2026-08-27T08:16:01-05:00 Human Resources Workstudy Assistant <div>The Human Resources Workstudy Assistant will assist staff within the Human Resources Office on various daily and long term processes. The Human Resources Workstudy Assistant will report to the Human Resources Generalist.<br><br><strong><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></strong></div> Human Resources https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/29767 2025-09-29T12:05:17-05:00 2025-09-29T12:05:18-05:00 Piano Accompanist - Part-Time <div>The piano accompanist provides support to the Department of Music through accompaniment on piano. The accompanist works closely with area coordinators and private lesson instructors during rehearsals and performances, which may occur during and outside the regular school day. The accompanist also serves as an instructional resource for music students. The piano accompanist reports to the Chair of the Music Department.<br><br><strong><em>This position is a part-time, as needed, hourly position. Days and hours assigned will vary based on departmental need at the time of assignment. As an hourly employee, use of a time clock is required.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31146 2026-06-05T16:34:27-05:00 2026-06-05T16:34:28-05:00 Assistant Director of Recruitment-Admissions <div>The Assistant Director of Recruitment-Admissions assists the Director and Associate Director of Admissions with initiatives and objectives to increase outreach and recruitment of prospective FTIC (First Time in College) students. This position’s primary focus will be on recruitment and admissions for UIW’s Broadway Campus programs, which includes traveling 20% of the time. The Assistant Director of Recruitment-Admissions reports to the Associate Director of Freshman Admissions.</div> Admissions https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31559 2026-07-30T11:05:31-05:00 2026-07-30T11:05:31-05:00 Laboratory/Virtual Reality Laboratory Student Assistant for the Clinical Learning Center (Work-Study) <div>The Laboratory/Virtual Reality Student Assistant supports the operation of the Ila Faye Miller School of Nursing and Health Professions (SNHP) Clinical Learning Center (CLC). The Laboratory/Virtual Reality Student Assistant supports laboratory, virtual reality laboratory, and clinical simulation activities for students enrolled in SHNP programs and works under the supervision of SNHP faculty and clinical teaching assistants. The Laboratory/Virtual Reality Student Assistant reports to the Simulation Director.<br><br><strong><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></strong><br><br><strong>Note: Due to the nature of this position, the selected candidate cannot be a nursing major or a health professions applicant.</strong></div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30898 2026-04-22T13:12:13-05:00 2026-04-22T13:12:14-05:00 LSAMP Peer Coach <div>The Peer Coach helps and guides students in the NSF LSAMP Scholar program via one-on-one meetings, authentic, personal connections, and group meetings with Scholars and other coaches. Peer coaches also assist in the annual Fall La Familia event, as well as with other events put on by the NSF LSAMP Alliance group. Peer Coach will report to the Peer Coach Coordinator.<br><br><em>Due to grant restrictions, this postion is not applicable for Nutrion majors.</em></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30819 2026-04-10T11:41:15-05:00 2026-04-10T11:41:15-05:00 Instructor for Entry-Level Doctor of Physical Therapy Program <div>The School of Rehabilitation Sciences invites part-time faculty candidates for Instructor for Entry-Level Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. This position will serve as a small group facilitator/tutor in the Physical Therapy Reasoning course series [~6 hours per week]. On a rare occasion, the person could serve as a teaching assistant in the Patient-Client Management course series. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching with service and professional activities as assigned. <br><br><strong>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the academic year.</strong></div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31326 2026-07-02T20:51:02-05:00 2026-07-02T20:51:03-05:00 Lifeguard (Student Position) <div>The Lifeguard monitors the safety of patrons and conditions of the pool. The Lifeguard reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br>This applicant pool will remain online for the 2026-2027 academic year and will be used to hire interested students as needed.</div><div><em><br></em><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31630 2026-08-14T17:36:44-05:00 2026-08-14T17:36:45-05:00 Student Employee Front Desk Assistant <div>Student Employee Front Desk Assistant will work to support the front desk staff at the Rosenberg School of Optometry. This position will report to the Assistant Clinic Support Manager.<br><br>Position will located at:<br>Datapoint Location, 9725 Datapoint Drive<br>Bowden Location, 2547 E. Commerce Street</div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31025 2026-05-13T21:44:27-05:00 2026-05-13T21:44:28-05:00 Student Sales Coordinator WORKSTUDY <div>The Student Sales Coordinator must be able to work in a team environment to handle sales inquiries both online, over the phone and in person. Sales coordinators must be familiar with regulations and policies to serve as liaisons for clients. The Student Sales Coordinator reports to the Sales Manager.</div> Facilities Events Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31495 2026-07-23T11:45:27-05:00 2026-07-23T11:45:27-05:00 New Student Programs Student Assistant <div>The New Student Programs Office Assistant provides customer service to students, faculty, and staff. The Office Assistant for New Student Programs works in conjunction with New Student Program peer mentors to better serve students and other members of the UIW community. The New Student Programs Office Assistant will report to the Director of New Student Programs.</div> New Student Programs https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31778 2026-09-04T10:58:07-05:00 2026-09-04T10:58:08-05:00 Graduate Student Worker for Institutional Research <div>The IR Graduate Student Worker will support the staff of the Office of Institutional Research with the completion of various projects which may include general surveys, the Institutional Profile Book, the maintenance of the electronic records, and other special data analysis projects.</div> Institutional Research https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31361 2026-07-07T08:30:13-05:00 2026-07-07T08:30:14-05:00 Advising Center- Student Worker <div>The Advising Center- Student Worker will assist with the daily routine office operations including, front desk and clerical support. The position requires providing effective communication through customer service and the ability to multi-task. This position will report to the Administrative Assistant and the Director of Undergraduate Advising. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></div> Academic Advising https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31728 2026-08-27T08:39:58-05:00 2026-08-27T08:39:58-05:00 Military and Veterans Services Specialist & School Certifying Official <div>The Military and Veteran Services Specialist &amp; School Certifying Official serves as a primary point of contact for military-affiliated students at UIW, providing exceptional customer service and administering U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Department of Defense (DoD) Tuition Assistance, and other educational benefits. The Military and Veteran Services Specialist &amp; School Certifying Official reports to the Assistant Director of the Military &amp; Veteran Center.<br><strong><em><br>This is an on-main-campus position, not eligible for remote work.</em></strong></div> Military & Veteran Affairs https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/29984 2025-11-13T11:40:14-06:00 2025-11-13T11:40:14-06:00 Assistant Professor, Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program <div>The entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program invites full-time, 12-month, non-tenured-track faculty candidates for Assistant Professor, Doctor of Occupational Therapy to teach in a variety of areas within the School of Rehabilitation Sciences. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarship, service, and professional activities. The Assistant Professor, Doctor of Occupational Therapy reports to the OTD Program Director.</div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31199 2026-06-16T21:45:19-05:00 2026-06-16T21:45:20-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Sports Medicine Administrative Assistant <div>Graduate Assistant for the Sports Medicine Department (Athletic Training), performs duties that include: managing the EMR system; managing athletic training rooms, and performing other duties as assigned. The Graduate Assistant Sports Medicine Department (Athletic Training) reports directly to the Associate Director of Athletics-Sports Medicine.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31567 2026-07-30T11:50:25-05:00 2026-07-30T11:50:26-05:00 Broadcasting Graduate Assistant <div>The University of the Incarnate Word is seeking qualified applicants for the position of Athletics Broadcasting Graduate Assistant. The Broadcasting Graduate Assistant is responsible for duties included but not limited to all aspects of broadcasting: set up, on-air play by play/color analysis, and clean up with the goal of creating, managing, and maintaining content that strategically enhances the brand of the University of the Incarnate Word in all external communications. The Broadcasting Graduate Assistant reports to Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to UIW graduate students only.</em></div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30943 2026-04-30T16:09:23-05:00 2026-04-30T16:09:23-05:00 Peer Tutor <div>The Peer Tutor provides academic tutoring and/or writing assistance to undergraduate UIW students individually and in groups, as qualified and will perform other center-related duties when not tutoring (see essential functions). Peer Tutors are assigned to specific disciplines based on qualifications. The Peers Tutors report to Director, Learning Support Services.</div> Learning Support Center https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31785 2026-09-04T14:14:33-05:00 2026-09-04T14:14:33-05:00 Track and Field Graduate Assistant for Sprints/Distance <div>The Graduate Assistant provides support to the Head Coach in all aspects of academic success, coaching, strength, conditioning, recruiting, planning of practice, organization of team meetings, scheduling and trip management. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Head Track and Field Coach. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW grauate students.</em></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30826 2026-04-13T11:00:50-05:00 2026-04-13T11:00:50-05:00 Lecturer in Mathematics <div>The School of Mathematics, Science and Engineering is seeking part-time faculty candidates for the position of Lecturer-Mathematics. Position teaches mathematics courses which may include: developmental mathematics, college algebra, college geometry, introduction to probability and statistics, precalculus, or calculus. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching with service and professional activities as assigned. <br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31328 2026-07-02T22:18:07-05:00 2026-07-02T22:18:07-05:00 Personal Trainer for Sports and Wellness (Student Position) (Student) <div>The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness is responsible for conducting orientations to the gym, introductions to fitness and plans, basic fitness assessments, and screenings. The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br>This applicant pool will remain online for the 2026-2027 academic year and will be used to hire interested students as needed.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31649 2026-08-18T13:28:40-05:00 2026-08-18T13:28:41-05:00 Lecturer in English <div>The Department of English invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer of English within the College of Humanities Arts and Social Studies. The Lecturer in English teaches Composition I, Composition II, and World Literature Studies in the UIW core. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online during the 2026-2027 academic year and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31027 2026-05-13T21:52:18-05:00 2026-05-13T21:52:18-05:00 Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant <div>The University of the Incarnate Word is seeking qualified applicants for the position of Athletics Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant. The Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting with the day-to-day facilities and operations of the Athletic Department. The position will report to the Assistant Athletic Director for Administration.<br><br>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31497 2026-07-23T11:51:24-05:00 2026-07-23T11:51:24-05:00 Student Worker - SOM Office of the Dean <div>The Student Assistant will provide administrative and research support to the School of Osteopathic Medicine’s Director of Accreditation and Professional Development for the Office of Professional Development (OPD), focusing on maintaining online resources in the SOM Learning Management System (LMS) and gathering information on professional development trends.<br><br>While the position supports UIWSOM, the workspace is located in the Provost’s Office in the Slattery Leadership Center on the Broadway Campus. The student will check in and out with the Academic Affairs Business Manager, who will then coordinate hours with the Senior Director at the SOM.<br><br>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students<br>who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30952 2026-05-06T08:47:47-05:00 2026-05-06T08:47:47-05:00 Student Assistant for the Artful Worship Program <div>The Student Assistant for the Artful Worship Program provides vital research and program support for a multi-year, arts-based faith formation initiative centered on the Catholic imagination. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Program Coordinator.</div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31374 2026-07-08T09:53:26-05:00 2026-07-08T09:53:27-05:00 Red the Cardinal - UIW Mascot <div>As Red the Cardinal, the official mascot of the University of the Incarnate Word, you will serve as an enthusiastic and engaging ambassador for the university. This role requires a positive, energetic, and professional demeanor while representing UIW at a variety of campus and community events. Responsibilities include wearing the mascot costume and interacting with diverse audiences to promote school spirit, foster community engagement, and enhance the university’s public image. Red the Cardinal reports to the Advertising, Branding and Licensing Mangager.</div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31731 2026-08-27T11:50:19-05:00 2026-08-27T11:50:20-05:00 Director of Advancement-St. Anthony Catholic High School <div>The Director of Advancement for St. Anthony Catholic High School (SACHS) provides leadership and strategy in advancement efforts which are in line with the Catholic mission of SACHS. Specifically, position is responsible for implementing and maintaining a comprehensive advancement program to include oversight of all fundraising, volunteer coordination, marketing, communications, and alumni relations. The Director of Advancement reports directly to the Principal and works collaboratively with school administration and UIW.<br><br><em>St. Anthony Catholic High School prepares young men and women for positions of responsibility and leadership through a college preparatory curriculum based on Catholic values and traditions.</em></div> St. Anthony Catholic High School https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30473 2026-02-25T12:06:30-06:00 2026-02-25T12:06:31-06:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice (Acute Care-Non Tenure Track) <div>The Department of Pharmacy Practice invites full-time faculty candidates for Assistant or Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice within the Feik School of Pharmacy. This <em>non-tenure track</em> faculty position will provide acute care clinical services at Baptist Medical Center in San Antonio, Texas.<br><br>Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarship, service and professional activities. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission.<br> <br><em>The Feik School of Pharmacy was founded in 2004 in recognition of the need to graduate a new generation of highly trained culturally-competent, caring pharmacists and patient advocates to serve communities across Texas and beyond. The School promotes full emergence of the student as a practitioner with a focus on a curricular integration, provision of high-quality pharmaceutical care, lifelong learning, appropriate use of technology, and opportunities for multi-cultural and multi-language development.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31225 2026-06-22T09:26:07-05:00 2026-06-22T09:26:08-05:00 Instructor for Nursing (Part-Time) <div>The Ila Faye Miller School of Nursing &amp; Health Professions invites candidates for part-time faculty for clinical and lab instruction in fundamentals, adult health, maternal-child health (pediatrics and care of childbearing family), psychiatric-mental health, medical-surgical nursing, and community health in the undergraduate nursing program. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><em><br></em><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31570 2026-07-30T12:27:12-05:00 2026-07-30T12:27:13-05:00 Communication Arts Graduate Assistant <div>The Communications Arts Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting in Department of Communication Arts media production, special projects, and more. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Communication Arts Department Chair.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31499 2026-07-23T11:56:50-05:00 2026-07-23T11:56:51-05:00 Graduate Nutrition Laboratory/Teaching Assistant <div>The Nutrition Program at the University of the Incarnate Word is seeking graduate students to apply for the Graduate Laboratory/Teaching Assistant (TA). The Graduate Laboratory/Teaching Assistant (TA) in the Nutrition Program is responsible for the supervision of all laboratory (Food Laboratory and Nutrition Laboratory) activities and assists in teaching specific Nutrition courses. The Nutrition Program has multiple TA positions therefore teamwork and communication are essential attributes for the position. The Graduate Laboratory/Teaching Assistant reports to the Nutrition Department Chair.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30829 2026-04-13T11:32:10-05:00 2026-04-13T11:32:10-05:00 Lecturer in Engineering <div>The School of Mathematics, Science and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for the position of Lecturer in Engineering to teach undergraduate level courses. The department offers a Bachelor of Science Degree in Engineering with tracks in Management, Mechanical, Electrical, and Mechatronics. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31330 2026-07-02T22:28:28-05:00 2026-07-02T22:28:29-05:00 Women's Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) <div>The Women’s Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the Men’s Club Sports Basketball team during the Fall and Spring semesters. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to UIW graduate students.</em><br><br></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31673 2026-08-20T14:23:34-05:00 2026-08-20T14:23:35-05:00 Student Assistant for Testing Services <div>The Staff Assistant provides support to the Coordinator of Testing in the daily operations of the Testing Center. Serves as the first line of contact with students and faculty. Administers faculty make-up examinations, national computer based exams such as CLEP, THEA and HESI-A2. Assists Coordinator and Specialist during testing and supervises the day's exams as required. Assists Coordinator in creating reports. Serves as an information source to students and faculty about the services offered at University Testing Services.</div> Testing Services https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31062 2026-05-26T16:58:13-05:00 2026-05-26T16:58:13-05:00 Lecturer in History <div>The Department of History invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in History within the College of Humanities Arts and Social Studies. The Lecturer in History will teach survey courses in World History or United States History as needed by the department. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online during the academic year and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30959 2026-05-06T15:32:54-05:00 2026-05-06T15:32:55-05:00 Athletics Administration Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Athletics Administration Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) works with the Athletic Director and the Athletics Senior Staff on a daily basis to manage the administrative affairs of the department. The Athletics Administration Coordinator supports both external and internal functions of the department. Internally this position supports financial services. The Athletics Administration Coordinator supports the day-to-day leadership of UIW’s Division I Athletic Department.&nbsp; The Athletics Administration Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) reports to&nbsp;</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31429 2026-07-14T13:30:29-05:00 2026-07-14T13:30:29-05:00 Standardized Patient (Part-Time) <div>The Standardized Patient (SP) is trained to portray the role of a patient, family member, or other to allow student learners to practice physical exam skills, history taking skills, communication skills, and other exercises. The SP will often be physically examined by students and faculty as part of the medical students learning experience. The SP must maintain a professional manner when interacting with students, faculty, supervisors, peers, and UIW partners. The Standardized Patient reports to Clinical Outreach &amp; Standardized Patient Manager.<br><br><strong>The Standardized Patient (part-time) works on an as needed basis and may work a few times per year or a few times per month. This position is located at University of Incarnate Word’s School of Osteopathic Medicine at Brooks City Base in South San Antonio, TX.</strong></div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31734 2026-08-27T12:52:51-05:00 2026-08-27T12:52:52-05:00 Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant- Workstudy Student <div>The Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant support the office functions within the Feik School of Pharmacy Office of Student Affairs.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30479 2026-02-25T17:05:33-06:00 2026-02-25T17:05:34-06:00 Lecturer in Spanish <div>The Department of Modern Languages invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Spanish within the College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences. Position will teach first-year Spanish courses and/or any other Spanish courses as needed. <br><br>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and teaching responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching with service and professional activities as assigned.<em><br><br>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the academic year.</em></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31232 2026-06-22T12:21:04-05:00 2026-06-22T12:21:04-05:00 Clinical/Didactic Adjunct-Rosenberg School of Optometry (Part-time Faculty) <div>The Rosenberg School of Optometry (RSO) invites part-time faculty candidates for Clinical and/or Didactic Adjunct. This position may have a dual role of providing clinical patient care and instruction responsibilities. Position will oversee RSO Residents, Interns, and Students in clinical services within the RSO Clinical Network. Position may also engage in classroom and/or laboratory instruction, consistent with the department’s needs. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br>The RSO Clinical Network includes the UIW Eye and Vision Care and Bowden Eye Care and Health Institute. Clinical services provided include the areas of Adult Care, Cornea and Contact Lenses, Dry Eye, Pediatric, Vision Therapy and Binocular Vision, Neuro Optometric Rehabilitation, Sports and Vision Enhancement, Ocular Disease and Retina Health, Low Vision and Rehabilitation, Vision Neurophysiology, and Peri-Operative.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the Academic Year 2026-2027.</em></strong></div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31575 2026-07-30T15:20:32-05:00 2026-07-30T15:20:32-05:00 Athletics Development - Student Assistant <div>The Athletics Development - Student Assistant assists and supports the Cardinals Club development team through event, hospitality, and donor experience support. The Student Assistant reports to Sr. Director of Development – Athletics.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Development https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31098 2026-05-30T10:54:14-05:00 2026-05-30T10:54:15-05:00 Graduate Assistant- Honors Program <div>The Graduate Assistant for the Honors Program assists the Director in planning and coordinating co-curricular programming and carrying out administrative functions of the program. The GA for the Honors Program reports directly to the Director of the Honors Program.</div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31521 2026-07-28T10:08:05-05:00 2026-07-28T10:08:06-05:00 Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry <div>Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry assist students in the Rosenberg School of Optometry with selected coursework during the 2026-2027 year. Tutoring is either done individually, in small groups or in a class-wide review session format depending on need. Tutors are being sought specifically for Clinical Optometry I, Optics, Anatomy, Neuroanatomy, Organ Pathology, and Ocular Anatomy and Physiology I. Academic Peer Tutors report to the Director, Academic Success. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current Rosenberg School of Optometry students who have completed the course(s) they wish to tutor with a grade of B or higher.</em></div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30834 2026-04-13T17:07:51-05:00 2026-04-13T17:07:52-05:00 Lecturer in Physics <div>The School of Math, Science, and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Physics in the Department of Atmospheric Science, Environmental Science, and Physics. Lecturers teach labs and/or lectures in undergraduate core physics courses including mechanics and/or electricity and magnetism. The department provides support courses in physics for various science disciplines across the campus where physics courses are required. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31332 2026-07-02T22:40:48-05:00 2026-07-02T22:40:49-05:00 Natatorium Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Graduate Assistatant is responsible for operations of the UIWNatatorium: participates in and supervises daily life guard coverage, cleaning, maintenance and repair of equipment and facility (including dressing rooms). The Graduate Assistatant reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to UIW graduate students.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31711 2026-08-24T16:21:45-05:00 2026-08-24T16:21:45-05:00 Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor <div>The Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor is responsible for engaging in recruitment activities and providing direct support to prospective students with applications and application records up to initial university enrollment. As appropriate, position directs students to other university staff to aid with admissions processes. The Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor reports to the Director of Admissions.<br><br><strong><em>Note that this position involves 50% of traveling, primarily locally for admissions recruitment.</em></strong></div> Admissions https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30963 2026-05-06T16:18:45-05:00 2026-05-06T16:18:46-05:00 The Logos Student Newspaper Assistant Editor <div>The The Logos Student Newspaper Assistant Editor is the secondary person in charge of writing, editing, designing The Logos, a student-run newspaper. The Logos StudentNewsletter Assistant Editor reports to Faculty Advisor for The Logos.<br><br>This can be work study or student employment.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31438 2026-07-14T15:21:00-05:00 2026-07-14T15:21:00-05:00 Student Laboratory Technician <div>Student Lab Technicians assist the Biology and Chemistry Dept. Lab Coordinators in the making<br>of media &amp; solutions, cleaning &amp; stocking labs, setting up lab classrooms and perform<br>other tasks as assigned. Lab Technicians will have the opportunity to learn laboratory<br>skills and techniques that are useful to lab science employers across San Antonio and<br>the US. The student Lab Technicians report to the Biology Laboratory Director.<br><br>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students</div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31749 2026-08-31T13:16:12-05:00 2026-08-31T13:16:14-05:00 Program Coordinator-Artful Worship Grant <div>The Program Coordinator-Artful Worship Grant provides full-time coordination and operational leadership for Artful Worship: Inspiring Children's Faith Through the Catholic Imagination, a multi-year Lilly Endowment initiative exploring how literature, music, visual art, storytelling, and the creative imagination nurture children's faith. The Program Coordinator-Artful Worship Grant reports to the Program Director, Artful Worship.<br><br>The position is primarily based on campus. A limited hybrid work arrangement may be available after six months of successful employment.<br><br><strong><em>Note that this is a grant-funded position with funding approval through 07/01/2030. Note that grant can be extended or shortened based on fund availability and the needs of the department.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30629 2026-03-13T14:32:31-05:00 2026-03-13T14:32:31-05:00 Lecturer in Philosophy <div>The Philosophy Department invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Philosophy within the College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences. Position will teach undergraduate courses in Philosophy. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching with service and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in this discipline as needed during the academic year.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31240 2026-06-22T22:33:41-05:00 2026-06-22T22:33:41-05:00 Fashion Management - Student Assistant - 2026/2027 <div>The Student Assistant for Fashion Management primarily works as a teaching assistant in Fashion Studio classes and assists faculty and staff with day-to-day tasks as needed by the department. The Student Assistant reports to the Fashion Management Faculty.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31592 2026-08-05T11:14:06-05:00 2026-08-05T11:14:07-05:00 Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs <div>The Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs is responsible for providing administrative support for the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs in the Rosenberg School of Optometry (UIWRSO). The Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs reports to the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs.</div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31109 2026-06-02T09:53:27-05:00 2026-06-02T09:53:27-05:00 Study Abroad Student Assistant (Work-Study) <div>The Study Abroad Student Assistant is responsible for the Study Abroad social media and marketing design. On occasion, the Study Abroad Student Assistant covers the UIW Study Abroad office taking messages and scheduling advising appointments with students. The Study Abroad Student Assistant will report to the Study Abroad and Exchange Coordinator.<br><em><br>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Office of International Affairs https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31544 2026-07-28T17:54:06-05:00 2026-07-28T17:54:06-05:00 Ticket Operations Graduate Assistant <div>The Ticket Operations Graduate Assistant assists with the implementation of our strategic plan to sell season and group tickets in football, volleyball, men’s and women’s basketball, baseball, and softball. The Ticketing Graduate Assistant reports to Coordinator of Ticket Operations.</div> Development https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30843 2026-04-13T17:58:52-05:00 2026-04-13T17:58:52-05:00 Lecturer in Nutrition <div>The School of Math Science and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Nutrition. Position will teach courses in Nutrition and Human Performance. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned. <br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain open and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31334 2026-07-02T22:57:29-05:00 2026-07-02T22:57:30-05:00 eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) <div>The eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the eSports team during the Fall and Spring semesters. eSports offers competitions at the Club Sport level in the following games: Smash Bros, Overwatch, League of Legends, Rocket League, Counter Strike: Global Offensive, Tom Clancy’s Rainbow Six Siege, Dragon Ball FighterZ, Street Fighter V and others. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program. <br><br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31714 2026-08-25T09:13:33-05:00 2026-08-25T09:13:33-05:00 Systems Analyst/Programmer <div>The Systems Analyst/Programmer is responsible for providing support in maintaining academic and student-facing platforms, including learning management, CRM, and student advising systems. The Systems Analyst/Programmer reports to the Associate Director of Enterprise Support.</div> Enterprise Applications https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31612 2026-08-10T16:56:51-05:00 2026-08-10T16:56:51-05:00 Accountant <div>The Accountant position is responsible for performing routine and complex accounting and analytical work requiring professional knowledge of the theory and practice of recording, classifying, examining, analyzing accounting records and financial transactions, and generating and monitoring financial reports. The Accountant position reports to the Accounting Manager.</div> Comptroller's Office https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30999 2026-05-11T14:49:30-05:00 2026-05-11T14:49:31-05:00 Clinical Faculty, SOM (Part-time) <div>The Department of OPPI (Osteopathic Principals, Practices, &amp; Integration) invites<strong> </strong>part-time faculty candidates for Clinical Faculty, within the School of Osteopathic Medicine (UIWSOM) at University of the Incarnate Word. The faculty member will operate within the UIWSOM framework of lifelong learning through collaborative scholarship, innovative educational excellence, and learner-centered curricula.<br><br>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<strong><br><br></strong><strong><em>This position teaches out of the UIW's Brooks City Base Campus located at 7615 Kennedy Hill, San Antonio, TX 78235.</em></strong><br><br></div><div><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31444 2026-07-14T16:28:10-05:00 2026-07-14T16:28:11-05:00 Men's Basketball Graduate Assistant <div>The Men’s Basketball Graduate Assistant is responsible for duties including but not limited to assistance with travel plans, set up for games &amp; practices, managing equipment, game and practice video, on-court duties, social media, community service, and organizing team events. The Men’s Basketball Graduate Assistant reports to the Head Men's Basketball Coach.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31754 2026-09-01T07:20:41-05:00 2026-09-01T07:20:41-05:00 Student Library Assistant for School of Osteopathic Medicine (Brooks Campus) <div>The Student Assistant for School of Osteopathic Medicine (Brooks Campus) is responsible for providing basic circulation assistance. The Student Assistant reports to the Director of Library Services.</div> Library Services https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30668 2026-03-18T17:58:47-05:00 2026-03-18T17:58:48-05:00 UIWtv Student Broadcasting News Director (2026-2027) <div>The UIWtv Student Broadcasting News Director (ND) is responsible for all on-air Newscast. The station promotes education while serving the university as a positive, reliable, and entertaining source of campus news, sports, and events. The UIWtv Student Broadcasting News Director reports to the COMM/FILM faculty.<br><br>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31242 2026-06-23T09:58:14-05:00 2026-06-23T09:58:15-05:00 Research Compliance Coordinator <div>The Research Compliance Coordinator is responsible for ensuring compliance with federal and state research regulations, institutional policies, and best practices. This position provides specialized regulatory expertise and administrative support to the UIW research community in support of several research compliance areas, including, but not limited to: protecting human subjects in research; managing conflicts of interest in research; training in the responsible conduct of research; and education in research ethics and research compliance. The Research Compliance Coordinator reports to the Director of Research Operations.</div> Research & Graduate Education https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31112 2026-06-02T10:03:02-05:00 2026-06-02T10:03:02-05:00 Student Office Assistant School of Rehabilitation Sciences <div>The student office assistant provides assistance primarily to the Office of Academic Success and Student Affairs within the School of Rehabilitation Sciences. May provide some assistance within the dean's administrative area as needed. The student office assistant reports to Student Affairs Coordinator.</div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31547 2026-07-29T08:27:19-05:00 2026-07-29T08:27:19-05:00 Intramural Sports Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Intramural Sports Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for planning, implementing, facilitating and evaluating a comprehensive Intramural Sports program. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness. <br><br><br><em>This is a student position open to current graduate UIW students.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30846 2026-04-13T18:23:19-05:00 2026-04-13T18:23:19-05:00 Lecturer in Environmental Science <div>The School of Math, Science, and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Environmental Science in the Department of Atmospheric Science, Environmental Science, and Physics. The Lecturer will present in-person labs/or lectures in undergraduate, introductory-level environmental science courses. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31336 2026-07-02T23:15:46-05:00 2026-07-02T23:15:47-05:00 Help Desk Student Technician <div>The Help Desk Student Technician provides Level 1 phone and remote IT support to the UIW community on the Main Campus. The Help Desk Student Technician is also responsible for providing clients with Level 1 hardware and software support. The Help Desk Student Technician reports to the Help Desk Manager. <br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></strong></div> Digital Infrastructure, Operations, & Security https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31717 2026-08-25T10:00:03-05:00 2026-08-25T10:00:04-05:00 Lecturer Criminal Justice-SPS <div>The School of Professional Studies invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer, Criminal Justice. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the academic year beginning summer 2026. Note that part-time faculty are assigned for one term at a time.</em></strong></div> School of Professional Studies https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31255 2026-06-24T10:29:36-05:00 2026-06-24T10:29:37-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Pathology (Part-Time) <div>The Department of Applied Biomedical Sciences invites part-time faculty candidates for Assistant/Associate Professor of Pathology at the School of Osteopathic Medicine (UIWSOM) at the University of the Incarnate Word . This non-tenure track faculty position will teach Pathology to osteopathic medical students within the DO curriculum.<br><br></div><div>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarship, service and professional activities.<br><br></div><div>The faculty member will operate within the UIWSOM framework of lifelong learning through collaborative scholarship, innovative educational excellence, and learner-centered curricula. The faculty member will be expected to facilitate small interactive group sessions and engage in case-based and large group discussions. It is strongly preferred that research activity be consistent with the UIWSOM research/scholarly activity strategic plan, including medical education research.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>This position teaches out of the UIW’s Brooks City Base Campus located at 7615 Kennedy Hill, San Antonio, TX 78235.</em></strong></div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31616 2026-08-11T16:44:21-05:00 2026-08-11T16:44:22-05:00 Administrative Assistant-Pharmacy <div>The Administrative Assistant is responsible for supporting the Pharmacy Practice and Experiential Education Programs Departments, both faculty and administrators. This position regularly works with securing appropriate documentation from students to ensure rotation compliance. The Administrative Assistant to Pharmacy Practice Dept. and Experiential Education Programs reports to the Assistant Dean, Department Chair of Pharmacy Practice and Professor.</div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31014 2026-05-12T18:31:12-05:00 2026-05-12T18:31:13-05:00 Student Lab Technician <div>The Student Lab Technician works in a basic science research laboratory, operates lab equipment, performs experimental procedures, and collects and summarizes research data. Responsibilities include assisting or conducting a variety of scientific experiments and research projects of limited complexity, collecting, evaluating, and interpreting data for clinical and diagnostic research. The Student Lab Technician reports to professor.</div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31447 2026-07-14T16:34:21-05:00 2026-07-14T16:34:21-05:00 Graduate Assistant of Baseball Operations <div>The Director of Baseball Operations (Graduate Assistant) assists with team travel logistics, p-card reconciliations, ordering apparel and equipment, and other administrative duties as assigned by the Head Baseball Coach.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31757 2026-09-01T09:04:09-05:00 2026-09-01T09:04:09-05:00 Student Assistant for Admissions Processing <div>The Student Assistant for Admissions Processing assists the processing specialists with all tasks, processes, and documents received as part of a student application. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Admissions Processing.</div><div>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</div> Admissions https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30670 2026-03-18T18:09:01-05:00 2026-03-18T18:09:02-05:00 UIWtv Student Broadcasting Program Director (2026-2027) <div>The UIWtv Program Director (PD) is responsible for the programming of the UIWtv station. The PD manages personnel and oversees all stories and programs related to UIWtv. The PD conducts rehearsals and assists in pre-production for live programs. The UIWtv Program Director reports to the COMM/FILM Faculty, Senior Instructor.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31116 2026-06-02T10:24:44-05:00 2026-06-02T10:24:45-05:00 TEAM RED Campus Engagement Student Assistant (Work-Study) <div>Team Red Work-Study employees support the Office of Campus Engagement by providing customer service to students, faculty, and staff while assisting with the planning and execution of student events. They collaborate with the Campus Life Office and maintain an understanding of campus services and resources to effectively assist the campus community. Work-study employees report directly to the Coordinator of Campus Engagement. <br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Campus Engagement https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31556 2026-07-30T10:15:20-05:00 2026-07-30T10:15:21-05:00 Lab Teaching Assistant for Rosenberg School of Optometry (Student Position) <div>The Lab Teaching Assistant (TA) assists current RSO students with lab tutoring for the following courses: Clinical Optometry I, Clinical Optometry II, Clinical Optometry III, Clinical Optometry IV, Neuroanatomy and any other labs as needed. This position reports to the Director, Student Success.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW 3rd year/4th year Rosenberg School of Optometry students.</em></div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30873 2026-04-16T16:39:15-05:00 2026-04-16T16:39:15-05:00 Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) will assist the with strength and conditioning for all UIW athletes. The Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) reports to the Head Strength and Conditioning Coach.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31338 2026-07-02T23:45:01-05:00 2026-07-02T23:45:01-05:00 Employee and Student Wellness Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>Employee and Student Wellness Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for assisting in the development, direction, implementation and evaluation of a comprehensive Employee and Student Wellness program. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.</div><div><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31719 2026-08-25T10:03:08-05:00 2026-08-25T10:03:09-05:00 Lecturer in Finance-SPS <div>The School of Professional Studies invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Finance. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned. <br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for 2026-2027 academic year. Note that part-time faculty are assigned for one term at a time.</em></strong></div> School of Professional Studies https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31317 2026-07-02T08:22:01-05:00 2026-07-02T08:22:02-05:00 Student Assistant for UIW Athletics Ticket Office <div>The Student Assistant for UIW Athletics Ticket Office assists the Coordinator of Ticketing with scanning game-day tickets, distributing will-call tickets, and handling game-day sales for Football, Volleyball, Men’s and Women’s Basketball, Baseball, and Softball. This position reports to the Coordinator of Ticket Sales.</div> Development https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31627 2026-08-14T17:34:57-05:00 2026-08-14T17:34:58-05:00 Work Study Student Assistant-America Reads/Counts Tutor <div>The Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability will provide academic math and reading tutoring support to local elementary and middle school campuses as part of the America Reads/America Counts Federal Work-Study Program (AR/AC Tutors). AR/AC Tutors will provide tutoring for assigned individuals or small groups in PK-8th grade regularly.Students will be assigned to a tutor by the campus coordinator. This position will report to the Director, Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability. <br><br><strong><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></strong></div> Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31022 2026-05-13T21:23:35-05:00 2026-05-13T21:23:35-05:00 RLHO Graduate Assistant - Residential Experience <div>The <em>RLHO Graduate Assistant</em> is considered essential personnel and works under the supervision of the Residence Life &amp; Housing Operations (RLHO) full-time staff to support students and student staff by providing a holistic, high-quality residential living experience. Expectations include ability to recruit, train, and mentor student staff on community policies, operational procedures, crisis response, and professional development.<br><br></div><div>As a 12-month live-in leadership member, the <strong><em>GA-Residential Experience</em></strong><em> </em>is primarily responsible for recognition efforts, departmental marketing and media, and assessing the residential experience</div> Residence Life & Housing Operations https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31470 2026-07-17T10:49:09-05:00 2026-07-17T10:49:09-05:00 Student Special Events Crew Member (Work- Study <div>The Special Events Crew Members assist with daily operations of set up and breakdown of event equipment such as tables, chairs, and platforms, and deliver and transport office and dormitory furniture. The Special Events Crew Member reports to the Coordinator of Facilities Events.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></strong></div> Facilities Events Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31767 2026-09-03T09:02:37-05:00 2026-09-03T09:02:38-05:00 IT Project Manager/Business Analyst <div>The IT Project Manager/Business Analyst is responsible for collaborating with cross-functional and technical teams across domestic and international UIW sites to facilitate business analysis and management of project activities. Key responsibilities include managing project operations to support the successful implementation of technological processes and/or system improvements. The IT Project Manager/Business Analyst reports to the Assistant Director of Global Technology Operations and Project Management.</div> Digital Transformation & Innovation https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30684 2026-03-23T10:04:24-05:00 2026-03-23T10:04:25-05:00 Lecturer in Religious Studies <div>The Department of Religious Studies is seeking part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Religious Studies within the College of Humanities, Arts, &amp; Social Science. Position will teach undergraduate courses in Religious Studies. This is a part-time, non-tenure-track appointment. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31722 2026-08-25T17:19:51-05:00 2026-08-25T17:19:52-05:00 Business Operations Manager <div>The Business Operations Manager serves as a key member of the School of Nursing and Health Professions (SNHP) team and supports the Dean in overseeing the school's financial, operational, and administrative activities, as well as collaborates with program chairs, directors, and faculty as appropriate. This position is responsible for budget planning and monitoring, operational coordination, compliance reporting, staff supervision, and special projects that support the school's academic mission and strategic goals. The Business Operations Manager reports to the Dean, School of Nursing and Health Professions.</div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31136 2026-06-05T09:20:55-05:00 2026-06-05T09:20:56-05:00 Laboratory Student Assistant (Work Study/Student Worker) <div>The Laboratory Student Assistant will assist in the weekly operations of biochemistry research and teaching laboratories. Typical duties will include washing and setting-up laboratory glassware, making solutions, performing inventory of laboratory supplies, and assisting biochemistry faculty with other laboratory preparation duties as assigned. The Laboratory Student Assistant will report to the Chemistry Lab Manager.<br><br>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31558 2026-07-30T11:05:10-05:00 2026-07-30T11:05:10-05:00 Substitute Teacher Pool - St. Anthony Catholic High School <div>St. Anthony Catholic High School is seeking substitute teachers for the 2025-2026 academic school year. Substitute Teachers report to the Principal and Dean of Student Affairs.<br><br>St. Anthony Catholic High School prepares young men and women for positions of responsibility and leadership through a college preparatory curriculum based on Catholic values and traditions.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire on an as-needed basis throughout the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> St. Anthony Catholic High School https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30896 2026-04-22T13:10:22-05:00 2026-04-22T13:10:23-05:00 Student Groundskeeper <div>Student Work-Study groundskeepers are responsible for maintaining the grounds and landscaping of assigned areas on all UIW campuses. This includes keeping UIW grounds areas clean and orderly, free of trash and debris. Groundskeepers report to Groundskeeper Supervisor.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31340 2026-07-02T23:48:33-05:00 2026-07-02T23:48:33-05:00 Natatorium Swim Lesson Coordinator (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Graduate Assistant – Swim Lesson Coordinator is responsible for coordinating and supporting the administration of the UIW Natatorium Swim Lesson Program. Primary responsibilities include scheduling and organizing swim lesson sessions, recruiting, training, supervising, and evaluating swim instructors, ensuring high-quality instruction and exceptional customer service, maintaining participant records, and assisting with program promotion and registration. The Graduate Assistant also supports daily natatorium operations as needed, including facility oversight, risk management, and ensuring a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for all participants. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to UIW graduate students.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30790 2026-03-31T15:55:18-05:00 2026-03-31T15:55:18-05:00 3D Animation & Game Design Student Tutor & Lab Monitor (2026-2027) <div>The 3D Animation &amp; Game Design Student Tutor and Lab Monitor is responsible for providing in-person and online tutoring for 3D Animation and Game Design courses (particularly Game Engines). This position reports to the ANGD Program Coordinator<br><br>This is a student position open to students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31321 2026-07-02T09:59:12-05:00 2026-07-02T09:59:12-05:00 Ecumenical/Interfaith Coordinator (Peer Ministry Intern) <div>The Ecumenical/Interfaith Coordinator serves as a Peer Ministry Intern (PMI) within University Mission and Ministry (UMM) to articulate the mission of the division by engaging university life through prayer, worship, outreach, faith development, and pastoral care. The Ecumenical/Interfaith Coordinator reports to the Ecumenical Interfaith Chaplain.</div> Office of Mission & Ministry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31629 2026-08-14T17:35:36-05:00 2026-08-14T17:35:37-05:00 Graduate Assistant for the Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability <div>The Graduate Assistant for the Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability will focus on organizing, researching, and supporting transformative social justice programming and services that will enhance the University’s and the Center’s initiatives. The Graduate Assistant reports to the&nbsp; Director-Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability. <br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW master’s or doctoral students.</em></strong></div> Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31024 2026-05-13T21:38:56-05:00 2026-05-13T21:38:56-05:00 Student Assistant for Skyroom Operations <div>The Student Assistant for Skyroom Operations will serve in the Skyroom Operations Office and in the Skyroom for events, handling operations of events or meetings that take place in the Rosenberg Skyroom. The Student Assistant for Skyroom Operations reports to</div><div>The Skyroom Operations Manager.</div> Facilities Events Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31487 2026-07-21T09:29:58-05:00 2026-07-21T09:29:59-05:00 Student Assistant for Admissions Office <div>The Student Assistant for the Admissions Office assists with all tasks, processes and events<br>of the Office of Admissions. The Student Assistant provides excellent customer service to prospective students, their families, and the community as a whole. The Student Assistant reports to the Assistant Director of Campus Events. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></div> Admissions https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31777 2026-09-04T10:47:43-05:00 2026-09-04T10:47:43-05:00 Student Music Minister <div>The Student Music Minister is part of a team that serves at the 11 AM Mass as a member of and musical leader for the Laudate Choir. As a leadership team member of the Music Ministry, the Music Minister also serves at major university liturgies and prayer events sponsored by University Mission and Ministry.</div> Office of Mission & Ministry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31342 2026-07-02T23:52:28-05:00 2026-07-02T23:52:29-05:00 Club Sport Physical Therapist (Graduate Assistant) <div>Club Sport Physical Therapist (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for assisting in the development, direction, and evaluation of a comprehensive sports medicine Club Sports program. Coordinates and delivers therapy and training programs to meet individual fitness, recovery, and health services to various club student-athletes. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br>This position is open to current UIW Graduate students.&nbsp;<br><br></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31727 2026-08-27T08:20:09-05:00 2026-08-27T08:20:10-05:00 Lecturer in Economics <div>The Department of Economics invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Economics within the H-E-B School of Business and Administration. This faculty position will teach undergraduate and/or graduate<strong> </strong>courses in economics. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated discipline as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> HEB School of Business and Administration https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/29977 2025-11-13T11:31:45-06:00 2025-11-13T11:31:46-06:00 Clinical Faculty, Full Time - Osteopathic Principles, Practices and Integration (OPPI) <div>UIWSOM is seeking outstanding applicants for a full-time clinical faculty position to participate in a variety of activities within the Clinical &amp; Applied Science Education (CASE) department, with a focus on osteopathic principles, practices, and integration (OPPI). Participation in clinical practice activities is negotiable. The faculty position reports to the Chair of the CASE department.<br><br></div><div>The faculty member will have responsibilities that include curricular development and support, faculty development in the area of osteopathic philosophy, delivery of osteopathic patient care, and community engagement with physicians. The faculty member will be expected to facilitate small interactive group sessions and engage in case-based and large group discussions. The candidate will operate within the UIWSOM framework of lifelong learning through collaborative scholarship, innovative educational excellence and learner-centered curricula.</div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31198 2026-06-16T21:43:08-05:00 2026-06-16T21:43:09-05:00 Student Assistant for Accounts Payable <div>The Student Assistant for Accounts Payable will help support the Accounts Payable Office by performing clerical duties and other duties assigned. The Student Assistant for Accounts Payable reports to Senior Accounts Payable Technician.</div> Accounts Payable https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31565 2026-07-30T11:37:23-05:00 2026-07-30T11:37:24-05:00 Student Worker (Work-Study) <div>The Student Worker supports the School of Nursing and Health Professions faculty and staff in their daily duties. This position reports to the Admissions Coordinator.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30900 2026-04-22T13:23:25-05:00 2026-04-22T13:23:26-05:00 Senior Resident Assistant <div>The Senior Resident Assistant (SRA) position is a student leader role responsible for providing support and assistance to RLHO Administrators within a housing community comprised of one or more residence hall buildings. This student has been a Resident Assistant and wishes to promote a positive living &amp; learning environment. The Senior Resident Assistant (SRA) reports to a Residence Life Coordinator.</div> Residence Life & Housing Operations https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31782 2026-09-04T11:23:44-05:00 2026-09-04T11:23:45-05:00 Graduate Assistant -  UMM Media Ministry <div>The Graduate Assistant for UMM Media Ministry assists in producing and archiving various media for the promotion of events that support the mission of the university. Position will also assist in the mentoring and supervision of undergraduate Media Ministry Interns and volunteers. The Graduate Assistant for UMM Media Ministry reports to Director of Music Ministries and Liturgy. <br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> Office of Mission & Ministry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30824 2026-04-13T09:52:52-05:00 2026-04-13T09:52:52-05:00 Lecturer in Chemistry <div>The School of Mathematics, Science, and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Chemistry. Position presents lectures and/or labs in undergraduate chemistry courses and a variety of labs. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31327 2026-07-02T22:00:48-05:00 2026-07-02T22:00:49-05:00 Sports Ops Workers (Student Position) <div>The Sports Ops. Worker runs intramural sport and club sport events and promotions. Duties include promotions, scorekeeping, officiating, setting up and cleaning up of intramural and club sports events and programs. The Sports Operation Associate reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br><strong>This applicant pool will remain online for the 2026-2027 academic year and will be used to hire interested students as needed.</strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31634 2026-08-17T17:36:33-05:00 2026-08-17T17:36:33-05:00 Shipping/Receiving Warehouse Clerk <div>The Shipping and Receiving Warehouse Clerk will be responsible for incoming and outgoing shipments, verifying and maintaining records, preparing items for shipment and coordinating transportation arrangements. The Shipping and Receiving Warehouse Clerk reports to the Fixed Asset Specialist.</div> Shipping & Receiving https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31026 2026-05-13T21:49:44-05:00 2026-05-13T21:49:45-05:00 Communications Graduate Assistant <div>The Communications Graduate Assistant assists with different duties such as graphic design, social media management, digital advertising, and more. The Communications Graduate Assistant reports to the Assistant Director of Strategy and Marketing. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></div> Digital Strategy & Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31496 2026-07-23T11:48:48-05:00 2026-07-23T11:48:49-05:00 Student Assistant for Title IX (Work-Study) <div>The Student Assistant for Title IX will help support the Office of Title IX by performing general office duties and assisting in the planning and execution of programming. The Student Assistant for Title IX reports to the Director of Title IX. <br><br><strong><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are</em></strong><em> </em><strong><em>approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></strong></div> Title IX https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30946 2026-05-01T14:14:04-05:00 2026-05-01T14:14:05-05:00 Front Desk Staff <div>| The Front Desk Associate (Student Position) provides a welcoming and safe environment for all patrons of sports and wellness facilities, through high-level customer service. The Front Desk Associate reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br>This applicant pool will remain online for the 2025-2026 academic year and will be used to hire interested students as needed. <br><em><br></em><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31372 2026-07-08T09:26:49-05:00 2026-07-08T09:26:49-05:00 Pharmacy Student Tutor <div>The Pharmacy Student Tutor provides tutoring for P1 students in one or more courses in pharmacy calculations, pharmaceutics, physiology, biochemistry, and microbiology/immunology. This position reports to the Assistant Dean and Chair, Dept. of Pharm. Sc.<br><br><strong>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested UIW students as the need arises.</strong><br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW P2 pharmacy students.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31729 2026-08-27T09:32:57-05:00 2026-08-27T09:32:58-05:00 Writing & Learning Center Program Leader <div>The Writing and Learning Center (WLC) Program Leader is responsible for managing the daily operations of the Writing and Learning Center. The WLC Program Leader reports to the Director of Learning Support Services.</div> Learning Support Center https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30419 2026-02-16T16:25:00-06:00 2026-02-16T16:25:01-06:00 STAR—Student Trained in Advising & Registration <div>University Advising Center, STARs (Student Trained in Advising &amp; Registration) will assist their supervisor in supporting students with questions related to advising and registration resources, events and deadlines. In addition, STARs will aid in preparation and/or notation of advising appointments, and other office duties. This position will report to the Administrative Assistant and Director of the University Advising Center. <br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></div> Academic Advising https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31214 2026-06-18T09:03:57-05:00 2026-06-18T09:03:58-05:00 Artistic Swimming Graduate Assistant <div>The Graduate Assistant Artistic Swimming Coach will serve in all phases of a competitive artistic swimming program in accordance with US Collegiate, USA Artistic Swimming and University of Incarnate Word rules and regulations. The Graduate Assistant Artistic Swimming reports the the Head Swim Coach.</div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31568 2026-07-30T11:53:31-05:00 2026-07-30T11:53:32-05:00 Graduate Assistant- Athletics Marketing and Fan Engagement <div>The Graduate Assistant for Athletics Marketing and Fan Engagement will assist with game management, fan engagement, marketing, development/booster club, in-game promotions, etc. Graduate assistants are often assigned specific sports to oversee the marketing, fan engagement, script writing, music, in-game entertainment, etc., for that sport. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing.</div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30828 2026-04-13T11:13:16-05:00 2026-04-13T11:13:16-05:00 Lecturer in Biology <div>The School of Mathematics, Science, and Engineering is seeking part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Biology. The Lecturer in Biology presents lectures and/or labs in undergraduate core biology, including anatomy and physiology courses and a variety of labs. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31329 2026-07-02T22:24:26-05:00 2026-07-02T22:24:26-05:00 Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness (Student) <div>The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness is responsible for teaching classes for Sports and Wellness facilities, including water aerobics, group aerobics, group swim lessons, and individual swim lessons. The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31660 2026-08-19T13:43:11-05:00 2026-08-19T13:43:12-05:00 Student Assistant for Athletic Training (Work-Study) <div>The Student Assistant for Athletic Training will be responsible for the organization and management of athletic training services to various UIW student-athletes and teams under the supervision of the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine.</div><div><br></div><div><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31060 2026-05-26T16:23:25-05:00 2026-05-26T16:23:25-05:00 Journeyman Electrician <div>The Journeyman Electrician position is responsible for providing journeyman level skills and expertise in the installation, maintenance, preventive maintenance, remodeling, repair, servicing, and operation of the University’s electrical systems from 120 volts up to 480 volts. The position assembles, installs, and repairs circuitry, switchgear, distribution systems, and all related components, while planning layout and installs wiring for electrical fixtures, apparatus, and control equipment. The Journeyman Electrician is part of Facilities Management Department and reports to Master Electrician Supervisor.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31498 2026-07-23T11:53:21-05:00 2026-07-23T11:53:22-05:00 New Student Programs Peer Mentor <div>The New Student Programs (NSP) Peer Mentor is an upper-level student (1+ years completed as a post-high school college student) who assists in mentoring first-year in college and transfer students to acclimate themselves to the university setting. The NSP Peer Mentor helps connect new students with university resources, initiates social and academic opportunities, and helps provide a holistic experience for first-year and transfer students. The New Student Programs (NSP) Peer Mentor reports to the Director of New Student Programs.</div> New Student Programs https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30953 2026-05-06T08:50:07-05:00 2026-05-06T08:50:08-05:00 Student Optical Assistant <div>The Student Optical Assistant provides support to the optical staff at any of our locations. The Student Optical Assistant keeps the optical department organized and clean and assists optical sales and coordinates order pick-up. The student optical assistant reports to the Optical Manager.<br><br>This position will be assigned to either RSO Bowden Eye Care and Health Center (2547 E. Commerce St. SA. TX 78203), or UIW Eye Institute (9725 Datapoint Dr. SA. TX. 78229)</div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31391 2026-07-09T12:03:29-05:00 2026-07-09T12:03:29-05:00 Student Pharmaceutics Lab Grader <div>The pharmaceutics lab grader will assist the pharmaceutics lab faculty with grading of lab assignments.The pharmaceutics lab grader reports to the Assistant Dean and Chair, Dept. of Pharm. Sc.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW P3 pharmacy students.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31733 2026-08-27T12:44:07-05:00 2026-08-27T12:44:08-05:00 Student Assistant for Financial Assistance (Work-Study) <div>The student assistant will assist the Office of Financial Assistance with the efficient daily operations of the department. This position reports to the Financial Assistant Advisor.<br><br><em>This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program.</em> <em>Note that students can work a maximum of 20 hours per week.</em></div> Financial Assistance https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30478 2026-02-25T16:03:15-06:00 2026-02-25T16:03:15-06:00 Clinical Professor of Optometry-Open Rank <div>The Rosenberg School of Optometry invites full-time, non-tenure track, faculty candidates for Clinical Professor of Optometry-Open Rank. The Clinical Professor is expected to conduct classroom and clinical laboratory teaching in optometry theory and the clinical examination course series, consistent with the department's needs. This position may have responsibilities in the areas of ocular disease, pediatrics, and/or low vision.<br><br>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarship, service, and professional activities.<br><br><strong><em>Academic credentials and experience of finalist will determine final rank-Senior Clinical Instructor, Assistant Clinical Professor, Associate Clinical Professor, and Full Clinical Professor.</em></strong></div> Rosenberg School of Optometry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31229 2026-06-22T10:05:36-05:00 2026-06-22T10:05:37-05:00 Interior Design Part-Time Lecturer <div>The Interior Design Program invites part-time faculty candidates for Interior Design Lecturer within the School of Media &amp; Design. Position will teach undergraduate courses in Interior Design, to include, studio and seminar courses, ensuring implementation of CIDA standards in all courses taught. Integration of a variety of digital media into Design Studios is expected.<br><br>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31571 2026-07-30T12:28:23-05:00 2026-07-30T12:28:24-05:00 Film Production Student Assistant <div>The Film Production Student Assistant supports the daily operations of the Film program by assisting faculty, staff, and students with equipment management, studio organization, production support, and media-related projects. This position provides students with hands-on experience using professional filmmaking equipment while developing organizational, technical, and collaborative skills essential to careers in the film and media industries.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31515 2026-07-28T07:51:16-05:00 2026-07-28T07:51:16-05:00 Skyroom Operations Management GA <div>The Operations Management GA for Rosenberg Skyroom will serve in the Skyroom Operations Office and in the Skyroom for events, handling operations of events or meetings that take place in the Rosenberg Skyroom. The Operations Management GA for Rosenberg Skyroom reports to</div><div>The Skyroom Operations Manager.</div> Facilities Events Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30831 2026-04-13T11:42:19-05:00 2026-04-13T11:42:20-05:00 Lecturer in Computer Information Systems & Cyber Security Systems <div>The School of Mathematics, Science and Engineering invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Computer Information Systems &amp; Cyber Security Systems. The School offers a Bachelor of Science Degree in Computer Information Systems or Cyber Security Systems.&nbsp; In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31331 2026-07-02T22:34:03-05:00 2026-07-02T22:34:04-05:00 Men's Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) <div>The Men’s Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the Men’s Club Sports Basketball team during the Fall and Spring semesters. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to UIW graduate students.</em></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31677 2026-08-21T16:56:51-05:00 2026-08-21T16:56:51-05:00 Instructor in Athletic Training-Masters Program (Part-Time) <div>The School of Rehabilitation Sciences invites part-time faculty candidates for an Instructor in Athletic Training-Masters Program. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching with service and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed during the academic year or earlier.</strong></div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31068 2026-05-27T16:39:28-05:00 2026-05-27T16:39:29-05:00 Media Minister (Student Position) <div>The Media Minister serves as a Peer Ministry Intern (PMI) within University Mission and Ministry (UMM) to actuate the mission of the division by engaging university life through prayer, liturgy, outreach, faith development, and pastoral care. This position reports to the Director of Music Ministries and Liturgy.<br><br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></div> Office of Mission & Ministry https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30962 2026-05-06T16:15:30-05:00 2026-05-06T16:15:31-05:00 The Logos Student Newspaper Editor <div>The Logos Student Newspaper Editor is the primary person in charge of writing, editing, designing The Logos, the student-run newspaper. The Logos Student Newspaper Editor reports to the Faculty Advisor for The Logos.<br><br>This can be work study or student employment.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31436 2026-07-14T15:06:53-05:00 2026-07-14T15:06:54-05:00 Box Office & Theatre Office Student Assistant <div>The Student Office Assistant is assigned to both the Box Office and the Theatre Department Office. In both offices, the student will perform administrative tasks necessary for the department as well as provide customer service for the patrons who attend UIW theatrical productions.</div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31736 2026-08-27T13:18:22-05:00 2026-08-27T13:18:23-05:00 Theatre Technician (Student Position) <div>Theatre technicians provide technical production support and assist in the preparation of performance spaces for the Theatre Arts Department’s production season.<br><br>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested UIW students as the need arises.<br><br>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30481 2026-02-25T17:40:21-06:00 2026-02-25T17:40:22-06:00 Lecturer in Voice <div>The Department of Music invites part-time faculty candidates for a Lecturer in Voice within the College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences. This faculty position will teach applied voice lessons and may also be asked to teach Singer's Workshop, Singing for Beginners, and other voice area courses as needed. Responsibilities also include recruitment and attendance at departmental studio hour and voice seminar on Thursdays from 1:30 to 2:45 p.m.<br><br>In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the university include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the academic year.</em></strong></div> College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31238 2026-06-22T18:41:00-05:00 2026-06-22T18:41:00-05:00 Kinesiology, Sport Management & Wellness Instructor (Part-Time) <div>The Ila Faye Miller School of Nursing &amp; Health Professions invites part-time faculty candidates for Instructor, Kinesiology, Sport Management, and Wellness. This position will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in respective areas. Note that part-time faculty are assigned for one term at a time. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated areas as needed during the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31581 2026-08-04T09:31:18-05:00 2026-08-04T09:31:19-05:00 Student Worker <div>The Office of Communication and Brand Marketing is looking for a work study student to support the office and its staff. Students in this position may be required to work independently and with minimal supervision on projects. This position reports to the department’s Administrative Assistant.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31106 2026-06-02T09:45:16-05:00 2026-06-02T09:45:17-05:00 Student Library Assistant <div>Student Library Assistant essential responsibilities include providing basic circulation assistance and troubleshooting minor photocopier, printer, and scanner problems. The Student Library Assistant reports to Library Assistant III Circulation Manager.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students.</em></div> Library Services https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31543 2026-07-28T17:42:56-05:00 2026-07-28T17:42:56-05:00 New Student Programs Graduate Assistant <div>The New Student Programs (NSP) Graduate Assistant supports the Director of New Student Programs in creating a welcoming and engaging transition experience for new students at the University of the Incarnate Word. Working closely with the Director, the Graduate Assistant helps plan, implement, and assess programs designed to foster student success and connection during their transition to the university.<br><br></div><div>In this role, the Graduate Assistant promotes New Student Programs services and resources, cultivates a sense of community among new students, and provides direct supervision, training, and support for the New Student Programs student staff.</div> New Student Programs https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30838 2026-04-13T17:34:01-05:00 2026-04-13T17:34:02-05:00 Lecturer in Atmospheric Science-Meteorology <div>The Department of Atmospheric Science, Environmental Science, and Physics invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Atmospheric Science in the School of Mathematics, Science &amp; Engineering. This position presents face-to-face labs and/or lectures in undergraduate meteorology courses including Meteorology, Synoptic, and Forecasting. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain open and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31333 2026-07-02T22:54:24-05:00 2026-07-02T22:54:24-05:00 Women's Club Volleyball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) <div>The Women’s Club Volleyball Coach (Graduate Assistant) will be responsible for coaching the Women’s Club Sports Volleyball team during the Fall and Spring semesters. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31712 2026-08-25T08:07:08-05:00 2026-08-25T08:07:09-05:00 Teacher Certification Officer/Assessment Coordinator <div>The Teacher Certification Officer/Assessment Coordinator is a full-time administrative position with the responsibility of managing the educator certification program of the Dreeben School of Education. The Teacher Certification Officer/Assessment Coordinator reports directly to the Director of Teacher Education, working collaboratively with the Dean of the Dreeben School of Education.</div> Dreeben School of Education https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31594 2026-08-06T10:32:11-05:00 2026-08-06T10:32:11-05:00 Research Associate <div>The Research Associate is responsible for assisting in faculty-led research, operating and maintaining scientific instrumentation, coordinating research activities, contributing to the teaching and training of students and research personnel, and ensuring compliance with research regulations and procedures for the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences. The role exercises independent judgment in troubleshooting experiments, supporting data integrity, and assisting with compliance‑related procedures under faculty direction. The Research Associate reports to the Assistant Dean/Chair of Pharmaceutical Sciences.<br><br><em>Note that this position is institutional funded, not dependent on grant-funding.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30988 2026-05-11T08:38:50-05:00 2026-05-11T08:38:51-05:00 Small Interactive Groups Facilitator, Part-time <div>The University of the Incarnate Word School of Osteopathic Medicine (UIWSOM) invites part-time faculty candidates for Small Interactive Groups Facilitator. This position is responsible for guiding and evaluating the SIGS process. Small Group Interactive Sessions (SIGS) are a cornerstone of the first two years of UIWSOM’s Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) curriculum. During the first two years, learners meet on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday mornings in small groups with a faculty process facilitator. Candidates who are selected for the position must successfully complete the SIGS facilitator training program. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission.</div><div><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.</em></strong></div> School of Osteopathic Medicine https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31439 2026-07-14T16:00:43-05:00 2026-07-14T16:00:44-05:00 RLHO Office Assistant-Student <div>The Student Office Assistant for the Department of Residence Life and Housing Operations provides administrative support, to include: filing; working on assigned projects; tours; and assisting with the daily operations of the offices. The Student Office Assistant reports to the Associate Director of Residence Life and HOusing Operations<br><br><br></div> Residence Life & Housing Operations https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31753 2026-08-31T17:03:26-05:00 2026-08-31T17:03:27-05:00 Assistant Women's Tennis Coach <div>The Assistant Women’s Tennis Coach supports the Head Coach and Director of Tennis in all aspects of operating a competitive NCAA Division I Women’s tennis program. The position plays a key role in fostering a culture of accountability, development, and competitive excellence consistent with UIW’s mission and Southland Conference standards. The Assistant Women’s Tennis Coach reports to the Head Coach and Director of Tennis.<br><br><strong><em>Note this position is funded for five years based on fundraising revenue with continuation depending upon fundraising success.</em></strong></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30666 2026-03-18T16:40:51-05:00 2026-03-18T16:40:52-05:00 UIWtv Student Broadcasting Operations Manager (2026-2027) <div>The UIWtv Operations Manager (OM) is responsible for the day-to-day operation of UIWtv. This position allows the Student Officer an opportunity to learn to deal with real-life production challenges and gain professional experience and receive hands-on experience for students with an interest in the production process and aesthetics of broadcast television. The UIWtv Operations Manager reports to Senior Instructor.&nbsp; The UIWtv Operations Manager reports to the COMM/FILM Faculty, Senior Instructor.<br><br><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></strong></div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31241 2026-06-22T22:39:30-05:00 2026-06-22T22:39:31-05:00 Interior Design - Student Lab Assistant (2026-27 Academic Year) <div>The Student Lab Assistant for Interior Design assists faculty and staff in their duties to support the daily operations of the Interior Design Department</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31111 2026-06-02T10:02:16-05:00 2026-06-02T10:02:16-05:00 Student Library Assistant <div>Student Library Assistant essential responsibilities include providing basic circulation assistance and troubleshooting minor photocopier, printer, and scanner problems. The Student Library Assistant reports to the Health Sciences Liaison Librarian.<br><br><strong>This position is located at 9160 Gilbeau Rd, San Antonio, Texas.</strong></div><div><br>This position is funded by the <strong>Federal Work-Study</strong> program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the<strong> Federal Work-Study Program</strong>.</div> School of Rehabilitation Sciences https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31545 2026-07-28T17:56:15-05:00 2026-07-28T17:56:16-05:00 Video Production Assistant <div>The Video Production Assistant is responsible for producing the live streaming and coverage of all home UIW athletic events. This includes the setup and take down of equipment and producing a quality stream while incorporating all sponsorship assets. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing.</div> Communications & Brand Marketing https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30844 2026-04-13T18:09:08-05:00 2026-04-13T18:09:08-05:00 Lecturer in Broadcast Meteorology <div>The Department of Atmospheric Science, Environmental Science, and Physics invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Broadcast Meteorology within the School of Math Science and Engineering. This position presents face-to-face labs and/or lectures in undergraduate broadcast meteorology courses. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain open and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for the 2026-2027 academic year.</em></strong></div> School of Mathematics, Science & Engineering https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31335 2026-07-02T23:13:08-05:00 2026-07-02T23:13:08-05:00 Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) <div>The Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) for the Wellness Center is the technician supervisor and is responsible for completing maintenance and repairs of equipment and facility Wellness Center. Duties for this position include daily cleaning of facility, equipment, and dressing rooms and overseeing technician staff. The Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness.</div> Sports & Wellness https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31716 2026-08-25T09:58:05-05:00 2026-08-25T09:58:06-05:00 Lecturer in Biology-SPS <div>The School of Professional Studies invites part-time faculty candidates for Lecturer in Biology. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties and responsibilities of part-time faculty members at the University include teaching and professional activities as assigned.<br><br><strong><em>This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty as needed for 2026-2027 academic year. Note that part-time faculty are assigned for one term at a time.</em></strong></div> School of Professional Studies https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31615 2026-08-11T11:17:34-05:00 2026-08-11T11:17:34-05:00 Student Assistant for Student Engagement Center <div>The Student Assistant for the Student Engagement Center (SEC) assists the SEC Staff with event management, the SEC Information Desk, and the Red’s Pub Check-Out Desk within the Student Engagement Center. The Student Assistant reports to the Events Operating Manager.<br><br><em>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment.</em></div> Facilities Events Management https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31011 2026-05-12T14:21:44-05:00 2026-05-12T14:21:44-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice (Acute Care, Tenure-Track) <div>The Department of Pharmacy Practice invites full-time faculty candidates for Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice (Acute Care) within the Feik School of Pharmacy. This is a 12-month tenure-track faculty position providing clinical services to acutely ill patients at CHRISTUS Santa Rosa Hospital - Westover Hills in San Antonio, Texas. Accordingly, position works collaboratively with the family medicine faculty and residents of the CHRISTUS Health/TXAM FM residency program. <br><br>Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarship, service and professional activities. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission.<br><em><br>The Feik School of Pharmacy was founded in 2004 in recognition of the need to graduate a new generation of highly trained culturally-competent, caring pharmacists and patient advocates to serve communities across Texas and beyond. The School promotes full emergence of the student as a practitioner with a focus on a curricular integration, provision of high-quality pharmaceutical care, lifelong learning, appropriate use of technology, and opportunities for multi-cultural and multi-language development.</em></div> Feik School of Pharmacy https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31446 2026-07-14T16:32:58-05:00 2026-07-14T16:32:59-05:00 Graduate Assistant for Softball Operations <div>The Graduate Assistant for Softball Operations (Graduate Assistant) is a non-coaching position that is responsible for duties including, but not limited to, all aspects of day-to-day functions for the UIW Women's Softball team. The Graduate Assistant for Softball Operations reports to the Head Softball Coach. <br><br><strong><br></strong><strong><em>This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students.</em></strong></div> Athletics https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31756 2026-09-01T09:02:53-05:00 2026-09-01T09:02:54-05:00 Graduate Assistant- Admissions Processor <div>The Student Assistant for Admissions Processing assists the processing specialists with all tasks, processes, and documents received as part of a student application. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Admissions Processing.</div> Admissions https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30669 2026-03-18T18:06:11-05:00 2026-03-18T18:06:11-05:00 UIWtv Student Broadcasting Multimedia Journalist (2026-2027) <div>The Student Broadcasting Multimedia Journalist (MMJ) is responsible for writing, filming, and editing news stories for the live broadcast, website, and social media. The Student Broadcasting Multimedia Journalist reports to the Senior Instructor.&nbsp; The Student Broadcasting Multimedia Journalist reports the COMM/FILM faculty.<br><strong><em><br>This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment</em></strong>.</div> School of Media & Design https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31252 2026-06-24T09:51:29-05:00 2026-06-24T09:51:31-05:00 CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist <div>The CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist will play a pivotal role in driving the growth and success of the CRNA program by effectively managing the recruitment, enrollment and compliance processes from initial inquiries to successful matriculation of graduate registered nurses. The role encompasses building clinical partnerships, marketing and social media engagement, credentialing and compliance for all external and internal agencies as well as facilitating student clinical rotation schedules and monitoring program compliance with accreditation standards. This dynamic position works closely with CRNA program administration to collect, monitor, analyze and synthesize data for program outcomes. The CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist reports to the CRNA Program Director.</div> ILA Faye Miller School of Nursing & Health Prof"
    },
