er members of the UIW community. The New Student Programs Office Assistant will report to the Director of New Student Programs. View Details Bookmark Graduate Student Worker for Institutional Research STU1680PO Institutional Research Student The IR Graduate Student Worker will support the staff of the Office of Institutional Research with the completion of various projects which may include general surveys, the Institutional Profile Book, the maintenance of the electronic records, and other special data analysis projects. View Details Bookmark Instructor for Entry-Level Doctor of Physical Therapy Program UN1021PO School of Rehabilitation Sciences University Faculty The School of Rehabilitation Sciences invites part-time faculty candidates for Instructor for Entry-Level Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. This position will serve as a small group facilitator/tutor in the Physical Therapy Reasoning course series [~6 hours per week]. On a rare occasion, the person could serve as a teaching assistant in the Patient-Client Management course series. In all matt... View Details Bookmark Peer Tutor STU1564PO Learning Support Center Student The Peer Tutor provides academic tutoring and/or writing assistance to undergraduate UIW students individually and in groups, as qualified and will perform other center-related duties when not tutoring (see essential functions). Peer Tutors are assigned to specific disciplines based on qualifications. The Peers Tutors report to Director, Learning Support Services. View Details Bookmark Military and Veterans Services Specialist & School Certifying Official AS2305PO Military & Veteran Affairs Administrator / Staff The Military and Veteran Services Specialist & School Certifying Official serves as a primary point of contact for military-affiliated students at UIW, providing exceptional customer service and administering U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Department of Defense (DoD) Tuition Assistance, and other educational benefits. The Military and Veteran Services Specialist & School Cert... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program UN821PO School of Rehabilitation Sciences University Faculty The entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program invites full-time, 12-month, non-tenured-track faculty candidates for Assistant Professor, Doctor of Occupational Therapy to teach in a variety of areas within the School of Rehabilitation Sciences. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. Official duties ... View Details Bookmark Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant STU1586PO Athletics Student The University of the Incarnate Word is seeking qualified applicants for the position of Athletics Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant. The Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting with the day-to-day facilities and operations of the Athletic Department. The position will report to the Assistant Athletic Director for Administration.This is a student pos... View Details Bookmark Communication Arts Graduate Assistant STU1668PO School of Media & Design Student The Communications Arts Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting in Department of Communication Arts media production, special projects, and more. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Communication Arts Department Chair. View Details Bookmark Student Assistant for the Artful Worship Program STU1573PO College of Humanities, Arts & Social Sciences Student The Student Assistant for the Artful Worship Program provides vital research and program support for a multi-year, arts-based faith formation initiative centered on the Catholic imagination. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Program Coordinator. View Details Bookmark Director of Advancement-St. Anthony Catholic High School HS418PO St. Anthony Catholic High School High School Positions The Director of Advancement for St. Anthony Catholic High School (SACHS) provides leadership and strategy in advancement efforts which are in line with the Catholic mission of SACHS. Specifically, position is responsible for implementing and maintaining a comprehensive advancement program to include oversight of all fundraising, volunteer coordination, marketing, communications, and alumni rela... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice (Acute Care-Non Tenure Track) UN990PO Feik School of Pharmacy University Faculty The Department of Pharmacy Practice invites full-time faculty candidates for Assistant or Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice within the Feik School of Pharmacy. This non-tenure track faculty position will provide acute care clinical services at Baptist Medical Center in San Antonio, Texas.Official duties and responsibilities of faculty members at the University include teaching, scholarsh... View Details Bookmark Student Assistant for Testing Services STU1527PO Testing Services Student The Staff Assistant provides support to the Coordinator of Testing in the daily operations of the Testing Center. Serves as the first line of contact with students and faculty. Administers faculty make-up examinations, national computer based exams such as CLEP, THEA and HESI-A2. Assists Coordinator and Specialist during testing and supervises the day’s exams as required. Assists Coordinator in... View Details Bookmark Women's Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) STU1616PO Sports & Wellness Student The Women’s Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the Men’s Club Sports Basketball team during the Fall and Spring semesters. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program.This is a student position open to UIW graduate students. View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 Next 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of 