    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31785": {
      "title": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Track and Field Graduate Assistant for Sprints/Distance",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Track and Field Graduate Assistant for Sprints/Distance Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Track and Field Graduate Assistant for Sprints/Distance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Track and Field Graduate Assistant for Sprints/Distance Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Graduate Assistant provides support to the Head Coach in all aspects of academic success, coaching, strength, conditioning, recruiting, planning of practice, organization of team meetings, scheduling and trip management. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Head Track and Field Coach. This is a student position open to current UIW grauate students. Essential Functions Oversee tip management, including driving. Assist with fundraising activities. Work with campus community and the Athletic Department staff in assisting student-athletes in the registration process who are members of the Track and Field programs. Assist in practice and match transportation. Provide tennis facility support maintenance. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or designee. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Good administrative skills. Excellent written and oral communication skills. High motivation with a capacity for independent work within the context of a goal-oriented environment. Possess good interpersonal and organizational skills. Display leadership skills. Ability to work independently and within a team-oriented environment. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW graduate student. Required Work Experience Track and Field coaching and/or intercollegiate competitive experience. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday – Friday up to 25 hours per week. Some weekends and holidays. Physical Demands Ability to lift equipment, tools, and/or materials weighing up to 25 pounds waist high. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1686PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Head Track and Field Coach Salary $2,100 + Tuition Waiver Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Student Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW graduate or doctoral student? Yes No * Please describe your Track and Field coaching and/or intercollegiate completitive experience. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
