    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31778": {
      "title": "Cardinal Talent",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Graduate Student Worker for Institutional Research Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Graduate Student Worker for Institutional Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Student Worker for Institutional Research Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The IR Graduate Student Worker will support the staff of the Office of Institutional Research with the completion of various projects which may include general surveys, the Institutional Profile Book, the maintenance of the electronic records, and other special data analysis projects. Essential Functions This Graduate Student Worker will support the Institutional Research staff by: Preparing survey results for analysis Providing data support for various projects submitted to IR Maintaining appropriate communications between UIW personnel and the Institutional Research director and staff, as appropriate. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Knowledgeable of Microsoft Office 365, including Word, Excel, etc. Demonstrate excellent written and verbal communication skills Be able to work as part of a collaborative team Demonstrated experience working in an office setting Demonstrated experience working with data sets, data quality, and data visualizations Be detail-oriented, self-directed, and willing to learn Knowledge of data collection and data integrity Knowledgable with statistical methods, research, and analysis techniques Knowledge with business intelligence software, such as Power BI or Tableau Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Must be currently enrolled as a full-time student in a graduate-level program at the University of the Incarnate Word. Required Work Experience N/A Preferred Qualifications At least 6 month Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations N/A Work Hours Maximum of 20 hours per week Physical Demands Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1680PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Institutional Research Manager Salary $13.50 per hour Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Professional Reference Contacts Optional Documents Other Document Student Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW graduate student, or have you been accepted to the UIW graduate program? No Yes, I am a current graduate student Yes, I have been accepted to the graduate program * Describe your most current experience, knowledge, and skills related to the job responsibilities. (Open Ended Question) * This is a part time position (1/2).  Are there any limits