    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31767": {
      "title": "Cardinal Talent",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | IT Project Manager/Business Analyst Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW IT Project Manager/Business Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title IT Project Manager/Business Analyst UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The IT Project Manager/Business Analyst is responsible for collaborating with cross-functional and technical teams across domestic and international UIW sites to facilitate business analysis and management of project activities. Key responsibilities include managing project operations to support the successful implementation of technological processes and/or system improvements. The IT Project Manager/Business Analyst reports to the Assistant Director of Global Technology Operations and Project Management. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Project Management Description of Job Duties Documents business requirements and translates needs into functional and technical specifications as part of project planning. Plans and assists with oversight of testing processes, defect identification, and problem resolution. Establishes and maintains strong relationships with campus partners and subject matter experts. Facilitates cross-functional meetings, records meeting minutes, and maintains document repository. Communicates regularly with project stakeholders and IT leadership regarding project status, risks, and issues. Prepares and maintains a repository of routine project status reports, user guides, training documents, and other project artifacts for stakeholders. Serves as project liaison to navigate technical challenges with project stakeholders to identify viable resolutions. Safeguards integrity of project artifacts and departmental document repository. Performs other duties as assigned. Job Duty Name Business Analysis Description of Job Duties Works with functional and technical teams to document current state, gaps, and future state to optimize process efficiency. Evaluates effect of process changes on business, systems, and integrated processes. Accesses vendor support sites to investigate and resolve support issues for business stakeholders. Writes and modifies reports utilizing reporting tools. Prepares and delivers business process models for technological solutions to document process roles, responsibilities, and process activities. Writes SQL queries to analyze and create end-user reports. Serves as subject matter expert in the continuous improvement of the business analysis methodology and application of business analysis tools. Processes and conducts system analysis. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to effectively work with minimal supervision. Strong skills in project management and business analysis methodologies. Experience of knowledge in Microsoft productivity tools. Strong skills in writing SQL queries to analyze and create end-user reports. Strong skills in writing and modifying reports utilizing reporting tools. Ability to effectively facilitate meetings involving both functional and technical teams. Ability to effectively coordinate project activities. Effective oral, written and non-verbal communication skills. Ability to effectively pivot communication style to address the needs of the audience and shifting priorities. Strong skills in critical thinking, time management, analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to work under pressure and meet targeted deadlines. A record of being flexible, accurate, detail-oriented, reliable, and self-motivated. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion in communicating confidential and/or sensitive information. Ability to effectively create training materials and presentations. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Information Systems, Information Technology, Computer Science, Business Administration, or relevant degree. Required Work Experience Three (3) years of professional experience in the field of business analysis. Note that complex internships will be considered. Two (2) years of professional complex project management experience facilitating business process reviews and documenting current processes, gaps, and desired future states. Note that complex internships will be considered. Two (2) years of experience developing and executing presentations for audiences with various technical levels within an organization. Preferred Qualifications Four (4) years of professional experience in the field of business analysis. Three (3) years experience facilitating business process reviews, documenting current processes, gaps, and desired future state. Three (3) years experience working in an educational/university environment. Three (3) experience working with Ellucian Banner Applications. Three (3) years of experience facilitating business process reviews and documenting outcomes. Three (3) years of experience using reporting tools such as Argos and Microsoft Power BI. Knowledge of higher education administrative areas and their function, such as the roles within the recruitment, admissions, registration, billing, and business/finance departments. Familiarity with higher education organizational structure, policies, and procedures. Business Analysis or Project Management certification. Bilingual in Spanish. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours Mon through Fri 8am to 5pm with extended hours as needed to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands Ability to regularly move about main campus and local satellite campuses to provide customer services as needed throughout the day. Ability to regularly move about campus to actively engage faculty, staff, and potential/current students, as well as attend meetings on and off campus. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2298PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Administrator (exempt) Desired Start Date 10/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Global Technology Operations and Project Management Salary $65,000-$70,000 Annualized Open Date 08/19/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least a Bachelors Degree in Computer Information Systems, Information Technology, Computer Science, Business Administration or relevant field? No Yes * How many years of professional experience do you have in the field of business analysis?  Note that complex internships will be considered. Less than 3 years of professional and/or complex internship experience 3 years including complex internships 3 years of professional experience 4 years of professional experience 5 years or more years of professional experience * How many years of professional complex project management experience do you have facilitating business process reviews and documenting current processes, gaps, and desired future states? Note that complex internships will be considered. Less than 2 years of professional and/or complex internship experience 2 years including complex internships 2 years of professional experience 3 years of professional experience 4 years of professional experience 5 or more years of professional experience * How many years of experience do you have developing and executing presentations for audiences with various technical levels within an organization? Less than 2 years 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 or more years 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
