    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31757": {
      "title": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Admissions Processing",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Admissions Processing Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Admissions Processing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Admissions Processing Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for Admissions Processing assists the processing specialists with all tasks, processes, and documents received as part of a student application. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Admissions Processing. This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment. Essential Functions Works in a fast paced, high-profile environment. Utilizes appropriate university databases to research student records. Indexes documents using university BDM system. Maintains confidentiality of student information and records. Provides excellent customer service to prospective students, their families, and the university community. Assists with opening and sorting incoming mail. Inputs incoming and outgoing mail in Admissions mail log. Assists with mail pick up and delivery between the Admissions office, UIW post office, and other campus offices. Assists with packaging and labeling of recruitment materials, student packets, counselor materials, and other mail-outs. Assists with facilitation of check-in for various admissions events. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Attention to detail. Moderate level of data entry speed and accuracy. Excellent interpersonal skills. Self-motivated with proper behavioral etiquette. Proficient in Microsoft Office 365 and OneDrive. Basic computer and office equipment skills. Ability to work well with others. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Strong verbal communication skills. Able to interact with staff in various positions (i.e., Directors, Vice Presidents, faculty, etc.). Ability to follow instructions and take direction. Ability to adhere to office dress code/uniform expectations. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student enrolled in at least half-time during the fall or spring semester. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Flexible shifts between the hours of 8am-5pm. Must be able to work flexible schedules during evenings and weekends when needed. Must be able to work Spring Break, some student holidays and Summer Sessions. Physical Demands Ability to regularly lift, push, and pull up to 20 lbs of recruiting materials. Ability to move about and actively engage with others during event preparation, execution of event, and post-event activities. Ability to sit for long periods of time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1682PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/07/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Admissions Processing Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 09/01/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
