nt interpersonal skills. Self-motivated with proper behavioral etiquette. Proficient in Microsoft Office 365 and OneDrive. Basic computer and office equipment skills. Ability to work well with others. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Strong verbal communication skills. Able to interact with staff in various positions (i.e., Directors, Vice Presidents, faculty, etc.). Ability to follow instructions and take direction. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, NCAA , Family Educational rights and privacy Act ( FERPA ). Required Education Current UIW graduate student. Required Work Experience N/A. Preferred Qualifications Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Office. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong attention to detail. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations N/A. Work Hours Flexible shifts between the hours of 8am-5pm. 20 Hours a week. Physical Demands Ability to regularly lift, push, and pull up to 20 lbs of recruiting materials. Ability to move about and actively engage with others during event preparation, execution of event, and post-event activities. Ability to sit for long periods of time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1681PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/07/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Admissions Processing Salary Tuition Waiver Open Date 09/01/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a UIW Graduate student? Yes No Applied - Awaiting Acceptance * What is the major of your Graduate Degree? (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
