    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31734": {
      "title": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant- Workstudy Student",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant- Workstudy Student Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant- Workstudy Student Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant- Workstudy Student Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Pharmacy Student Affairs Assistant support the office functions within the Feik School of Pharmacy Office of Student Affairs. This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program. Essential Functions Essential functions include: Greeting visitors to OSA , including prospective students and families, offering assistance where possible. Assist with preparation for FSOP Admissions Interview Days. Assist with preparation for group tours and visits or other events hosted by the Office of Student Affairs. Serve as a backup tour guide. Perform day to day clerical duties including organization of office materials, photocopying, restocking. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong interpersonal and communication skills (both written and verbal). Demonstrated organizational and time-management abilities. Attention to detail. Punctuality and dependability. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Appropriate attire according to Student Handbook. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of UIW FSOP . Required Education Current UIW student with a 2.5 GPA (or higher), awarded Financial Aid Work-Study eligibility. Required Work Experience No experience required. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Canva Knowledge of Microsoft 365 skills (Word, Excel, Powerpoint) Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Flexible hours available depending on the selected candidate’s schedule with a maximum of 20 hours per week. Hours available must fit within the range of Monday to Friday 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. with possibility for very occasional Saturday event hours. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 20 lbs. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1677PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) 09/01/2027 Reports to Administrative Assistant Salary 12.00 Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
