    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31733": {
      "title": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Financial Assistance (Work-Study)",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Financial Assistance (Work-Study) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Financial Assistance (Work-Study) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Financial Assistance (Work-Study) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The student assistant will assist the Office of Financial Assistance with the efficient daily operations of the department. This position reports to the Financial Assistant Advisor. This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program. Note that students can work a maximum of 20 hours per week. Essential Functions Support a friendly, student-oriented environment; Answer incoming phone calls/emails; Assist with information sessions if needed; Provide coverage during office meetings (approx. time 1 hour); Process deliveries from daily mail runs (open and date stamp); Provide support during Freshman Orientation in the summer; Assist advisors with tasks; Scan and file documents; Maintain confidentiality of student information; Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Basic knowledge of office skills (organizational skills, alphabetizing, filing, telephone, proper etiquette); Attention to detail; Excellent computer skills; Ability to learn quickly and efficiently; Knowledge of resources and services provided to students and alumni; Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures; Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program. Required Work Experience No previous work experience is required. Training is provided. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience with customer service in customer service. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours The Office of Financial Assistance is generally open Monday-Friday from 8am-5pm; Must be able to schedule work shift for a minimum of 2 hours within standard business hours. Physical Demands Ability to reach, squat, stoop and lift at least 10 lbs to organize and transport large quantities of documents and equipment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1678PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Financial Assistant Advisor Salary 11.00 per hour Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
