    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31729": {
      "title": "Cardinal Talent",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Writing &amp; Learning Center Program Leader Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Writing & Learning Center Program Leader Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title Writing & Learning Center Program Leader UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Writing and Learning Center ( WLC ) Program Leader is responsible for managing the daily operations of the Writing and Learning Center. The WLC Program Leader reports to the Director of Learning Support Services. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Daily Center Operations Description of Job Duties Ensures that the Learning Support lab functions smoothly. Manages writing tutor schedules, including regular tutoring schedule and workshops as requested. Provides coverage for front desk, as needed, to include answering phones, making appointments, and responding to emails. Serves as first line of contact for student and tutor concerns. Troubleshoots technology used for tutoring. Updates binder with comprehensive program information. Job Duty Name Student Supervision Description of Job Duties Works with leadership to hire and train student writing tutors and office assistants. Maintains program hiring records and communicates with applicants for both Learning Support programs. Coaches writing tutors on working with students. Oversees tutors’ development of writing resources. Job Duty Name Budget Tracking Description of Job Duties Tracks student wages. Maintains budget records. Updates leadership as needed. Job Duty Name Data and Reporting Description of Job Duties Edits writing tutor session reports for tone, clarity, and grammar errors. Sends professors weekly reports. Compiles semester data and runs reports as requested. Sends students reminders as needed. Job Duty Name Program Outreach Description of Job Duties Manages program outreach, to include events, flyers, and social media. Updates and maintains program web pages. Job Duty Name Workshops & Tutoring Description of Job Duties Leads writing workshops (typically in-class). Provides direct tutoring as needed. Job Duty Name Other Duties Description of Job Duties Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Outstanding oral and written communication; ability to adapt communication style to different audiences. Ability to adapt quickly to change and learn new technologies as needed. Ability to effectively handle multiple priorities. Ability to handle confidential information in a professional manner. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelor’s Degree. Required Work Experience One (1) year of experience working in academic support or closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in English or other writing-related field. Experience working in a writing center in higher education. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours Monday through Friday 8am to 5pm with extended hours as needed to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands Typical office environment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2307PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Administrator (exempt) Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of Learning Support Services Salary $46,500 Annualized Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Professional Reference Contacts Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest level of education you have achieved? Less than Bachelor's Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree PHD or higher * How many years of experience do you have working in academic support or closely related field? Less than 1 year 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 or more years * Describe your experience providing writing assistance in educational settings. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
