    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31726": {
      "title": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Human Resources Workstudy Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Human Resources Workstudy Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Human Resources Workstudy Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Human Resources Workstudy Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Human Resources Workstudy Assistant will assist staff within the Human Resources Office on various daily and long term processes. The Human Resources Workstudy Assistant will report to the Human Resources Generalist. This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program. Essential Functions Perform general clerical duties, including, but not limited to: photocopying, faxing, mailing, filing, processing mail, and responding to email. Assistance at the front desk, greeting visitors and delivering excellent customer service. Answers multiline phone system. Provide general University/Human Resources information. Assist new hires with completing appropriate new hire paperwork. Respond to applicant’s inquiries about job application utilizing the applicant tracking software. Submit background checks. Inter-campus deliveries. Assist with employee appreciation events. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Knowledgeable in Microsoft Word, Excel. Excellent customer service skills. Punctuality and dependability. Self-starter/ self-motivated. Excellent organizational skills. Excellent attention to detail. Problem-solving skills. Excellent people skills. ABility to maintain confidentiality. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to learn new software programs pertaining to office objectives. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA Required Education Current UIW student approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program. Required Work Experience Experience using Microsoft Office. Preferred Qualifications Prior office experience or in a similar setting. Typing and data entry skills. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Variable hours Monday through Friday 8:00am-5:00pm Physical Demands Typical for this position Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1599PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/07/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Sr. HR Generalist Salary $11/ hr. Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
