    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31711": {
      "title": "Cardinal Talent",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor is responsible for engaging in recruitment activities and providing direct support to prospective students with applications and application records up to initial university enrollment. As appropriate, position directs students to other university staff to aid with admissions processes. The Transfer and Graduate Admissions Counselor reports to the Director of Admissions. Note that this position involves 50% of traveling, primarily locally for admissions recruitment. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Territory Management Description of Job Duties Advises on admissions requirements, application procedures, and uses knowledge of university policies for evaluation of previous credit and career interest to prospective students. Responds to admissions inquiries in a timely manner with continued communication through the enrollment process, utilizing all available means of communication technology including email and texting platforms. Acts as an advocate for the prospective student to resolve application issues and coordinate with staff throughout the admissions process through initial enrollment. Tracks student and partner communications and enrollment results in an accurate and timely manner. Reviews prospective student documents toward an admission decision, conducting outreach via phone, email and texting platforms to move students through enrollment funnels appropriately. Works with processing and documents-receiving areas to update student records. Job Duty Name Recruiting Events Description of Job Duties Represents UIW Broadway Campus at various related internal and external meetings, community events, and college fairs to promote and showcase educational options, both in-person and virtually. Assists and attends on/off campus events to promote, engage and encourage prospective students toward enrollment at UIW . This requires extensive traveling locally and some travel within the state of Texas. Represents UIW Broadway Campus at community events and college fairs to promote and display educational options. Job Duty Name Relationship Building Description of Job Duties Serves as official admissions contact with the Office of Research and Graduate Studies and program coordinators. Maintains relationships with program directors, faculty, staff, and other departments. Cooperates with other UIW departments to assist prospective students and track progress of applicants through enrollment. Performs outreach to external sources, companies, and organizations to conduct group presentations and individualized communications on the features and benefits of university programs, both in-person and virtually. Job Duty Name Office Duties Description of Job Duties Assists prospective students visiting the campus with questions about the application and admission processes. Assists with the collection of documents required for admissions decisions. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to prioritize and plan work activities efficiently. Ability to identify and resolve problems in a timely manner, as well as adapt to shifting priorities. Ability to continuously build knowledge and skill set, as well as share knowledge/facilitate training with Counselors I and II. Strong customer service skills to meet customer needs as well as diffuse difficult/emotional customers while showing respect and sensitivity to cultural differences. Strong written communication skills to present information clearly and concisely with accuracy in spelling and grammar. Ability to consistently meet attendance policy and be at work, meetings and appointments on time. Ability to follow instructions, take ownership of responsibilities and keep commitments; ability to complete tasks on time or notify appropriate person in a timely manner when alternate plans are appropriate. Ability to take initiative in seeking increased responsibilities, taking independent actions and calculated risks, and asking for/offering help as appropriate, as well as engaging in self-development activities. Ability to travel extensively, primarily locally. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution. Required Work Experience Minimum of one (1) year of relevant professional experience in admissions or higher education recruitment. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of previous recruitment experience in higher education or in marketing. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Valid driver license with “Real ID” designation, as required for air travel, or ability to obtain by first day of employment. Must have a valid driver license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, and be at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW . Work Hours Mon-Fri 8am – 5pm; some evenings and weekends may be required to meet departmental needs, especially during peak periods. Physical Demands Ability to regularly lift, push, and pull up to 20lbs of recruiting materials. Ability to move about and actively engage with others during event preparation, execution of event, and post event activities. Ability to travel extensively primarily by vehicle. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2302PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Administrator (exempt) Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Associate Director of Transfer and Graduate Admissions Salary $45,000 Annualized Open Date 08/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest level of education you have achieved? Less than Bachelor's Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree PHD or higher * How many years of relevant professional experience do you have in admissions or higher education recruitment? Less than 1 year 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 or more years * Do you currently have a valid driver's license AND are you at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW? No Yes, I have a valid driver license and I am at least 21 years old * Do you currently have a valid driver license with \"Real Id\" designation as required for air travel? No Yes 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/bookmarks?posting_id=31711": {
      "title": "Cardinal Talent",
